UPDATE blog_posts SET content_en = '<h2>Introduction</h2><p>In the vibrant city of [Burnaby](/en/areas/burnaby/), BC, a family townhouse was in need of a modern makeover. Reno Stars took on the challenge to transform this space into a contemporary haven, perfect for a family with children. This case study explores the comprehensive renovation project, highlighting the key areas of transformation and the solutions implemented to overcome various challenges.</p><h2>Project Overview</h2><p>The [whole house renovation](/en/services/whole-house/) in Burnaby focused on cost-effective upgrades to enhance the living environment. The project included re-tiling the first floor, repainting the entire home, and replacing light fixtures. The overall budget ranged from $75,000 to $78,000, with a duration of 7 to 9 weeks.</p><img src="https://pub-b88db8c50fd64a9a87f60a4486a4a488.r2.dev/uploads/admin/social-ready-hero-mmmrl2j1.png" alt="Burnaby Whole House Renovation - Hero Image"><h3>Area 1: Two [Bathroom Renovation](/en/services/bathroom/)</h3><p>This part of the project involved a comprehensive renovation of two bathrooms. One bathroom was transformed from a bathtub to a modern shower, while the other featured elegant gray tiles and silver fixtures, complemented by custom frameless glass doors.</p><h4>Challenges</h4><p>The main challenge was to seamlessly integrate the new designs while ensuring functionality and comfort for the family.</p><h4>Our Solution</h4><p>We addressed these challenges by carefully planning the layout and selecting high-quality materials that enhance both aesthetics and usability.</p><h4>Before & After</h4><div><img src="https://pub-b88db8c50fd64a9a87f60a4486a4a488.r2.dev/uploads/admin/social-ready-before-1-mmmrl4n7.jpg" alt="Two Bathroom Renovation with Shower and Tub - Before Renovation 1"><img src="https://pub-b88db8c50fd64a9a87f60a4486a4a488.r2.dev/uploads/admin/social-ready-after-1-mmmrl4n7.jpg" alt="Modern bathroom featuring a glass shower, bathtub, and sleek gray tile walls."></div><div><img src="https://pub-b88db8c50fd64a9a87f60a4486a4a488.r2.dev/uploads/admin/social-ready-before-2-mmmrl4x9.jpg" alt="Two Bathroom Renovation with Shower and Tub - Before Renovation 2"><img src="https://pub-b88db8c50fd64a9a87f60a4486a4a488.r2.dev/uploads/admin/social-ready-after-2-mmmrl4x9.jpg" alt="Modern bathroom featuring a glass shower, sleek vanity, and bright lighting."></div><h3>Area 2: Modern [Kitchen Renovation](/en/services/kitchen/) | [Cabinet Refinishing](/en/services/cabinet/) | [Pre-Sale Renovation Advice](/en/services/realtor/)</h3><p>The kitchen renovation transformed the space into a modern culinary area. The project included repainting the cabinets, replacing the countertops with white quartz, and laying new tiles with a stylish grey pattern.</p><h4>Challenges</h4><p>One of the main challenges was coordinating the various materials and ensuring a cohesive modern design throughout the space.</p><h4>Our Solution</h4><p>To address this, we carefully selected materials that complemented each other and worked closely with the client to finalize the design details.</p><h4>Before & After</h4><div><img src="https://pub-b88db8c50fd64a9a87f60a4486a4a488.r2.dev/uploads/admin/social-ready-before-1-mmmrl5kz.jpg" alt="Modern Kitchen Renovation with New Cabinets and Countertops - Before Renovation 1"><img src="https://pub-b88db8c50fd64a9a87f60a4486a4a488.r2.dev/uploads/admin/social-ready-after-1-mmmrl5l0.jpg" alt="Modern kitchen with dark cabinetry, marble countertops, and stainless steel appliances."></div><div><img src="https://pub-b88db8c50fd64a9a87f60a4486a4a488.r2.dev/uploads/admin/social-ready-before-2-mmmrl5l0.jpg" alt="Modern Kitchen Renovation with New Cabinets and Countertops - Before Renovation 2"><img src="https://pub-b88db8c50fd64a9a87f60a4486a4a488.r2.dev/uploads/admin/social-ready-after-2-mmmrl5wf.jpg" alt="Bright, modern room with white walls, large windows, and marble flooring."></div><h2>Results & Key Takeaways</h2><p>The renovation resulted in a modern, inviting home that perfectly suits the family''s needs. The client expressed immense satisfaction with the transformation, appreciating the enhanced functionality and aesthetic appeal. This project underscores the importance of meticulous planning and quality material selection in achieving a seamless renovation.</p>



Whole-house renovations are also an ideal time to incorporate [accessible bathroom features](/services/accessible-bathroom/) such as grab bars, step-in showers, and wider doorways — future-proofing the home for years to come.


Many Metro Vancouver homeowners are also upgrading to a [heat pump HVAC system](/services/heat-pump-hvac/) during major renovations — providing both heating and cooling in one energy-efficient unit, and qualifying for BC Hydro rebates.
## Frequently Asked Questions

### How much does a [whole house renovation cost](/en/guides/whole-house-renovation-cost-vancouver/) for a Burnaby townhouse?
A whole house renovation for a Burnaby townhouse typically costs $35,000–$90,000 depending on scope. A modern makeover covering flooring, paint, kitchen update, and bathroom refreshes for a family townhouse runs $35,000–$60,000. A full gut renovation including structural changes, new kitchen, and all bathrooms can reach $90,000–$140,000. Burnaby renovation costs are in line with Metro Vancouver averages, with the primary variables being material grade and the extent of trade work required.

### How long does a family townhouse renovation take in Burnaby?
A comprehensive whole house renovation for a Burnaby family townhouse typically takes 8–14 weeks of active construction. Permit-required work (plumbing, electrical panel changes) adds 2–4 weeks for City of Burnaby approvals before construction begins. Strata approval for the alteration is typically required and takes 3–6 weeks. Total project timeline from contract signing to move-in: 3–5 months for a thorough renovation.

### Do I need strata approval to renovate my Burnaby townhouse?
Yes. Burnaby townhouse strata corporations require Alteration Approval for renovations affecting shared systems, structural elements, flooring (noise compliance), plumbing, and electrical. Your contractor submits a scope of work, insurance certificates, and WorkSafeBC compliance documentation to the strata council. The approval process typically takes 3–6 weeks. Starting the strata application process in parallel with contractor selection is the most efficient approach.

### What are the best renovations for a family with children in a Burnaby townhouse?
For families with children, the highest-impact improvements in Burnaby townhouses are: durable luxury vinyl plank or tile flooring throughout (handles heavy traffic, easy to clean), updated bathrooms with practical storage solutions, modern kitchen with expanded counter space and storage, and fresh neutral paint that photographs well. Safety improvements — updated electrical panels, grounded outlets, and secure stair railings — are worth addressing during any comprehensive renovation. Our [Critical Load Panel Installation](/en/services/critical-load-panel/) service upgrades your home electrical capacity for modern renovation demands.

### Why choose Reno Stars for a Burnaby townhouse renovation?
Reno Stars has completed multiple whole house renovations throughout Burnaby, with direct experience in Burnaby''s permit process and strata council requirements. Our fixed-contract pricing locks in your budget at signing. We coordinate all trades — flooring, painting, electrical, plumbing, tiling — under one contract with a dedicated project manager, eliminating the coordination burden on the homeowner. Older Metro Vancouver homes may also need our [Poly-B Pipe Replacement](/en/services/poly-b-replacement/) service to eliminate unsafe plastic piping. Burnaby clients consistently rate our projects 4.9/5 for on-time delivery and quality.

Also see: [Burnaby home renovation case study](/en/blog/burnaby-home-renovation-case-study/) | [BC Renovation Permits Guide](/en/blog/renovation-permits-bc-guide/) | [Vancouver Renovation Cost Guide 2026](/en/blog/renovation-cost-vancouver-2026-complete-guide/) | [How to Choose a Contractor](/en/blog/how-to-choose-renovation-contractor-vancouver/) | [Renovation Timeline Guide](/en/blog/renovation-timeline-how-long-does-each-project-take/)

### What specific work was completed in this Burnaby townhouse renovation?
This Burnaby townhouse renovation was completed within a $75,000–$78,000 budget over 7–9 weeks, covering four scope areas: re-tiling the entire first floor (replacing dated flooring with a consistent tile or hard-surface material throughout the living areas), repainting the entire home in a fresh colour scheme, replacing light fixtures throughout with contemporary fittings, and renovating both bathrooms. See our guide to [BC Strata Renovation Rules](/en/blog/strata-renovation-rules-vancouver/) for Metro Vancouver homeowners. The combination of flooring, painting, and light fixture replacement — applied across the whole home simultaneously — achieves the maximum visual transformation for the budget, as every surface the eye rests on in daily use has been updated. The two bathroom renovations provided the functional upgrade alongside the whole-home cosmetic refresh.


See our [verified five-star reviews](/en/reviews/) from Metro Vancouver homeowners.

