## Frequently Asked Questions

### What is the difference between stock, semi-custom, and custom kitchen cabinets in Vancouver?
Stock cabinets are pre-built in fixed standard sizes (3-inch increments) — IKEA SEKTION is the dominant stock system in Metro Vancouver. Semi-custom cabinets offer finer size increments and more finish options but are made-to-order from a manufacturer''s existing line. Custom cabinets are built from scratch to exact dimensions by a local cabinet shop. Typical costs for a medium kitchen: stock $3,000–$8,000, semi-custom $10,000–$20,000, custom $18,000–$45,000+.

### Is IKEA SEKTION a good choice for a Vancouver kitchen renovation?
IKEA SEKTION is an excellent choice for budget-conscious Vancouver kitchens — the box construction is solid, soft-close Blum hardware is included, and replacement parts are readily available. The main trade-offs are limited configuration flexibility in non-standard spaces, standard sizes that may leave awkward filler gaps, and visible box ends in open layouts. Budget for a professional kitchen designer and experienced IKEA installer to maximize what the system can do.

### How long do custom kitchen cabinets take to order in Metro Vancouver?
Custom cabinets from a Metro Vancouver cabinet shop typically take 6–10 weeks from final design approval to delivery. Semi-custom cabinets through a dealer run 4–8 weeks. IKEA SEKTION is available immediately from stock in Coquitlam or [Richmond](/en/areas/richmond/) stores. Lead times are the primary reason kitchen renovations require cabinet selection to happen well before any demolition begins — waiting until demo day to order cabinets adds 6–10 weeks to your project.

### What should I look for in a Vancouver kitchen cabinet installer?
IKEA cabinet installation is a distinct skill set from custom cabinet installation — verify the installer specializes in your system type. For custom cabinets, confirm the installer has worked with your specific cabinet maker before, as tolerances and mounting systems vary. Check for a valid Metro Vancouver business licence and active WorkSafeBC coverage. Ask for references from kitchens in homes with similar layouts — the difference between professional and amateur installation shows in level lines, consistent reveals, and door alignment.

### Is cabinet refacing or professional painting a worthwhile alternative to full replacement in Vancouver?
Cabinet spray painting by a professional costs $2,500–$5,000 and can dramatically refresh dated oak or builder-grade cabinets without replacement expense. Cabinet refacing (replacing doors and drawer fronts, wrapping boxes) runs $5,000–$12,000 versus $15,000–$40,000 for full replacement. Both options make economic sense when the existing box structure is solid and you only want a visual update. Full replacement is the right choice when you need to change the layout, the interior space does not meet your needs, or the boxes are structurally compromised.


### How much do kitchen cabinets cost in Metro Vancouver in 2026?

Kitchen cabinet costs in Metro Vancouver: Stock cabinets (big-box store, IKEA SEKTION, home centre): $12,000–$25,000 for an average kitchen including installation. Semi-custom cabinets (factory-built with size customization): $20,000–$40,000 installed. Custom cabinets (built-to-measure, local cabinet maker): $35,000–$70,000+ installed. Cabinet painting/refinishing of existing boxes: $4,000–$8,000. Cabinet refacing (new doors, drawer fronts, same boxes): $8,000–$15,000. Semi-custom represents the best value for most Metro Vancouver kitchens — better sizing flexibility than stock, significantly lower cost than fully custom.


