The highest-value improvements for Coquitlam condo resale are: kitchen update (new countertops, cabinet hardware or paint, modern backsplash), bathroom refresh (new vanity, tile, frameless mirror, updated fixtures), full flooring replacement with contemporary LVP or engineered hardwood, fresh neutral paint throughout, and updated lighting. In Coquitlam''s condo market, buyers strongly prefer move-in-ready units — renovation investment typically yields strong returns at listing time.

### How long does a pre-sale condo renovation take in Coquitlam?
A focused [pre-sale renovation](/en/services/realtor/) for a Coquitlam condo typically takes 4–8 weeks of active construction depending on scope. Comprehensive kitchen and bathroom renovations run toward 8 weeks; cosmetic-only refreshes (paint, flooring, fixtures) can be completed in 3–4 weeks. Strata approval for the alteration takes 3–6 weeks and must be obtained before construction begins. Coordinate with your real estate agent on the target listing date to work backwards to a realistic renovation start.

### Do I need strata approval for a pre-sale condo renovation in Coquitlam?
Yes — any renovation involving plumbing, electrical, flooring (noise bylaw compliance), or modifications to common property systems requires strata council Alteration Approval. Your contractor should prepare and submit the application package. Buyers of newly renovated condos will review the strata minutes during due diligence; having proper approvals in place is important for a clean transaction. Unpermitted work disclosed during the sale can become a negotiation liability.

### Why invest in renovation before listing rather than pricing lower?
In Coquitlam''s condo market, move-in-ready units consistently attract more buyers and close faster than equivalent unrenovated units priced at a discount. Buyers price in renovation uncertainty beyond the actual renovation cost — a dated unit priced $40,000 below market may still linger, while a renovated unit at market price often receives multiple offers. Renovation also lets you control the quality and finish level, rather than accepting whatever a buyer''s renovation allowance produces.

Related cost guide: [Whole-House Renovation Cost Vancouver 2026](/en/guides/whole-house-renovation-cost-vancouver/) | [Coquitlam pre-sale renovation guide](/en/blog/pre-sale-renovation-coquitlam-bc-2026/)

### What was the specific renovation scope for this Coquitlam pre-sale condo?
This Coquitlam pre-sale condo renovation was completed within a $21,000–$23,000 budget over 3–4 weeks. The comprehensive scope included: demolition of existing fixtures and finishes, new flooring throughout, lighting optimization, baseboard replacement, electrical and plumbing work, a full bathroom renovation, wall repairs, and complete painting of all spaces. Older Metro Vancouver homes may also need our [Poly-B Pipe Replacement](/en/services/poly-b-replacement/) service to eliminate unsafe plastic piping. This full-scope approach — addressing every surface the buyer will see — transforms a dated condo into a competitive listing. The combination of new flooring, fresh paint, lighting upgrades, and a renovated bathroom creates a cohesive, move-in-ready presentation that justifies the renovation investment at resale.


