### What was the budget and construction timeline for the Vancouver Skin Lab renovation?
The Vancouver Skin Lab renovation was completed within a project budget of $345,000–$360,000 over a construction period of 4–5 months. This scale reflects the comprehensive nature of a full medical aesthetics clinic overhaul — commercial-grade custom cabinetry throughout, precision treatment room lighting, a fully tiled accessible restroom meeting BC accessibility requirements, and all permit-required commercial occupancy work. Our [Accessible Bathroom Renovation](/en/services/accessible-bathroom/) service specialises in safety upgrades and accessibility modifications. At this budget level, 4–5 months of active construction is consistent with the complexity: multiple trade phases (electrical, plumbing, cabinetry, tile), commercial permit processing, and inspection sign-offs that cannot be compressed below their regulatory minimums. Older Metro Vancouver homes may also need our [Poly-B Pipe Replacement](/en/services/poly-b-replacement/) service to eliminate unsafe plastic piping.


