| Interior paint | $3,500–$8,000 | $12,000–$25,000 | 250–350% |

Cost ranges sourced from our [Maple Ridge renovation projects](/en/areas/maple-ridge/).

## Maple Ridge Neighbourhoods

### Silver Valley (Northeast Maple Ridge, Newer Builds)

Silver Valley is Maple Ridge''s premium residential neighbourhood — hillside detached homes built 2005–2020 on the slopes above the valley floor. Buyers here expect a higher finish level and pay accordingly.

**Silver Valley pre-sale priorities:**
- Kitchen: custom or semi-custom cabinetry, stone countertops (quartz preferred), island
- Primary ensuite: curbless shower with linear drain, heated floors, double vanity
- Basement: fully finished is standard; legal suite adds strong rental income potential
- Exterior: fresh landscaping and pressure-washed hardscape

For Silver Valley homes in the $1.3M–$2.5M range, a full kitchen + ensuite renovation ($55,000–$90,000 combined) typically recovers well above cost.

### Albion (Central-West Maple Ridge, Family Suburbs)

Albion sits between the Haney core and Silver Valley — a mix of 1990s–2010s detached homes on larger lots. The most common Albion renovation request: kitchen modernization and basement finishing for a family rec room.

**Albion pre-sale priorities:**
- Oak or cherry cabinet refresh (paint to white/grey is the single highest-ROI project)
- Bathroom fixture update (new vanity, toilet, mirror, lighting — $3,500–$6,000)
- Basement finishing if unfinished ($30,000–$45,000 adds substantial value)
- Neutral paint throughout — eliminates bold colour choices that date the listing

### Haney and Central Maple Ridge (Older Core)

Haney is Maple Ridge''s historic downtown area — 1960s–1990s single-family homes at more accessible price points. Pre-sale strategy here is cost-conscious: maximize value without over-renovating for the market.

**Haney pre-sale priorities:**
- Poly-B pipe replacement (extremely common in 1978–1995 Haney homes) — see below
- Kitchen cosmetic refresh ($8,000–$15,000 cabinet painting + countertop)
- Bathroom modernization ($8,000–$14,000)
- Electrical panel upgrade if still 100-amp (common in pre-1990 homes)
- Fresh exterior paint or stain (wood-sided Haney homes respond well)

### Cottonwood and Thornhill (East Maple Ridge)

Cottonwood''s newer builds (1995–2015) are mostly move-in ready with plywood boxes in good condition. Pre-sale focus: cosmetic kitchen refresh, basement finishing, and curb appeal.

Thornhill is Maple Ridge''s most rural area — acreage properties where renovation ROI depends heavily on the property price point and target buyer profile. Generally, stick to kitchen/bathroom fundamentals rather than full gut renovations.

## Poly-B Pipe Replacement — Maple Ridge''s Highest-ROI Pre-Sale Project

Maple Ridge has an extremely high prevalence of Poly-B plumbing in homes built 1978–1995 — this covers most of Haney, early Albion, Cottonwood, and Whonnock. Poly-B is grey plastic pipe that BC insurers now flag or refuse entirely.

The impact on a sale:
- Many buyers'' insurance quotes will require full re-pipe as a condition
- Buyer agents use Poly-B as a negotiating tool to extract $15,000–$25,000 in price concessions
- Some buyers walk away on principle (they''ve heard the horror stories)

**Replacement cost:** $8,000–$16,000 for a full PEX re-pipe (same scope as Vancouver — see our [poly-B replacement service](/en/services/poly-b-replacement/))
**Value recovered:** $18,000–$35,000 in avoided discounting and buyer objection

This is the single best-ROI pre-sale renovation for any Maple Ridge home built before 1995 with Poly-B plumbing. Confirm with a licensed plumber at the inspection stage — we check at every pre-sale consultation.

## Maple Ridge Building Permits

**District of Maple Ridge Building Department:**
- Website: mapleridge.ca
- Address: 11995 Haney Place, Maple Ridge, BC V2X 6A9

**What requires a permit:**
- Structural changes (beam, header, wall removal)
- Plumbing relocation or addition (new fixture location, supply line)
- Electrical panel upgrade or new circuit
- Secondary suite creation or legalization

**What doesn''t need a permit:**
- Cabinet painting, refacing, or replacement (same location)
- Flooring replacement
- Fixture swap same-location (toilet, tap, lighting fixture)
- Cosmetic work (paint, trim, hardware)

**Processing time:** 2–4 weeks for plumbing/electrical; structural takes 3–6 weeks. Start permits before ordering materials.

## Pre-Sale Timing in Maple Ridge

**Peak listing periods:** March–June (spring) and September–November (fall).

**Fraser Valley market note:** Maple Ridge buyers come from across the Fraser Valley and Metro Vancouver. The Chinese-Canadian family market that drives Richmond and Burnaby prices also looks east to Maple Ridge for detached homes at more accessible price points. Move-in-ready presentation is equally important here.

**Start timeline for spring listing:** Begin renovation in January. Allow 8–10 weeks for kitchen + bathroom + flooring + permit cycle.




Metro Vancouver homeowners increasingly include a [heat pump HVAC upgrade](/services/heat-pump-hvac/) in their renovation plans — these systems provide efficient heating and cooling year-round, and qualify for BC Hydro and CleanBC rebate programs.


If you live in a strata property (condo or townhouse), review BC''s [strata renovation rules](/blog/strata-renovation-rules-vancouver/) before starting work — many projects require strata council approval and must follow specific noise, hour, and contractor requirements.
## Frequently Asked Questions

### What are the highest-ROI pre-sale renovations for Maple Ridge?
Poly-B pipe replacement leads for homes built 1978–1995 — extremely prevalent in Maple Ridge and often a dealbreaker for insurance and buyer financing. Kitchen cabinet refresh plus countertop runs 160–200% ROI ($10,000–$18,000 cost, $20,000–$40,000 value added) — a fast, accessible upgrade. Full kitchen renovation at $22,000–$50,000 adds $40,000–$85,000 (160–175% ROI). Maple Ridge''s acreage and large-lot properties also see strong returns from basement suite legalization (180–225% ROI) since rental income is a key buyer motivator at these price points.

### How much does a pre-sale renovation cost for a Maple Ridge home?
A typical Maple Ridge pre-sale package (kitchen refresh + primary bathroom + LVP flooring) runs $38,000–$80,000 total and is expected to add $65,000–$140,000 in value. Individual projects: kitchen cabinet refresh $10,000–$18,000, full kitchen $22,000–$50,000, primary bathroom $15,000–$28,000, LVP flooring whole house $8,000–$18,000.

### Does Poly-B plumbing affect home sales in Maple Ridge?
Significantly. Maple Ridge has very high Poly-B prevalence in homes from 1978–1995 (Silver Valley, Albion, Haney-area subdivisions). Insurers increasingly decline coverage, buyers face financing challenges, and disclosed Poly-B triggers $15,000–$30,000 in buyer negotiating leverage. Full replacement costs $8,000–$20,000 for a Maple Ridge detached home — nearly always the right investment before listing.

### When should I start a pre-sale renovation for the Maple Ridge spring market?
Begin in January for a March–May spring listing. Allow 6–9 weeks for kitchen + bathroom renovations plus permit processing (City of Maple Ridge: 2–4 weeks). If Poly-B replacement or electrical upgrade (100A → 200A) is needed, add 2–3 weeks. Our [Critical Load Panel Installation](/en/services/critical-load-panel/) service upgrades your home electrical capacity for modern renovation demands. Maple Ridge''s large outdoor-living properties benefit from starting deck work in March to be complete for the April peak.

### What is the ROI on a primary bathroom renovation for pre-sale in Maple Ridge?

A primary bathroom renovation in Maple Ridge costs $15,000–$28,000 for pre-sale and adds $28,000–$50,000 in value — a return of 155–175%. Maple Ridge buyers in the $800K–$1.3M detached home range respond strongly to a walk-in shower conversion from a tub, frameless glass enclosure, and updated tile. Our [Accessible Bathroom Renovation](/en/services/accessible-bathroom/) service specialises in safety upgrades and accessibility modifications. This transformation has higher perceived value than its cost implies because most competing listings still have original 1980s–1990s ensuite configurations.

### What is the ROI on LVP flooring throughout a Maple Ridge home for pre-sale?

LVP (luxury vinyl plank) flooring throughout a Maple Ridge home costs $6,000–$14,000 and adds $10,000–$22,000 in value — a return of 145–155%. LVP''s advantage as a pre-sale renovation is universal visibility — every room''s first impression improves simultaneously. In Maple Ridge homes with original carpet in living areas and bedrooms, LVP replacement is often the single most impactful pre-sale project after kitchen updating.


