### Does financing affect my mortgage renewal?
A HELOC with the same lender usually has no impact. A second mortgage or refinance with a new lender can affect renewal terms. Always check with your existing lender before adding a second charge to your title.


### How does projected rental income help me qualify for a BC basement renovation HELOC?

BC lenders in 2026 allow qualified borrowers to add 50–70% of projected market rent to their qualifying income when applying for home equity financing to build a basement suite. Example: if your suite will rent for $2,000/month, a lender may credit $1,000–$1,400/month as additional qualifying income. This can meaningfully improve your Gross Debt Service (GDS) and Total Debt Service (TDS) ratios — the 39% GDS / 44% TDS thresholds that govern approval. The lender will require a market rent letter or appraisal confirming the projected rent is realistic.
## Ready to start planning?

Financing and construction go hand in hand. Getting a fixed-price quote from a licensed contractor early makes every financing application smoother (lenders like to see real numbers, not estimates). Reno Stars provides detailed fixed-price quotes with line items that match what most BC lenders need for their approval packages.

