Port Coquitlam (PoCo) sits at the eastern edge of Metro Vancouver''s urban core, offering detached homes at price points significantly below Coquitlam or Burnaby — while still benefiting from SkyTrain access via the Evergreen Extension through neighbouring Coquitlam. This combination has made PoCo increasingly attractive to Chinese-Canadian families seeking detached-home ownership at accessible price points ($950K–$1. Our [Accessible Bathroom Renovation](/en/services/accessible-bathroom/) service specialises in safety upgrades and accessibility modifications.6M), strong school options (Riverside Secondary, Archbishop Carney Catholic Secondary), and manageable commutes to employment centres.

## Port Coquitlam''s Submarkets

### Citadel Heights (Northwest PoCo)
PoCo''s most prestigious neighbourhood, featuring larger lots, panoramic views, and homes dating from the late 1980s to early 2000s. Chinese-Canadian families here expect premium finishes and the full complement of modern amenities.

**Citadel Heights buyer priorities:**
- Gourmet kitchen with full custom cabinetry, large island, and professional ducted range hood
- Master ensuite with soaker tub, frameless glass shower, and his-and-hers sinks
- Updated secondary bathrooms (minimum 2 full baths)
- Finished basement (recreation room, bedroom, full bath — secondary suite ideal)
- Well-maintained exterior with curb appeal

### Hyde Creek / Woodland Acres (East PoCo)
Established family neighbourhoods with homes from the 1970s–1990s. Many properties are reaching their renovation cycle and present excellent pre-sale opportunities — buyers willing to buy and renovate are priced out by move-in-ready equivalents elsewhere.

**Hyde Creek renovation priorities:**
- Poly-B pipe replacement (very common — 1978–1995 construction era)
- Electrical panel upgrade (100A → 200A)
- Kitchen modernization (countertop, cabinet doors, ventilation)
- Bathroom updates (flooring, fixtures, lighting)

### Riverwood (South PoCo, Near Mary Hill)
A mix of townhomes, condos, and detached homes surrounding Riverwood Golf & Country Club. Lower price point than Citadel Heights but strong demand from young families and commuters.

## Port Coquitlam Building Permits

City of Port Coquitlam Building Services: **604-927-5442**
Address: 2580 Shaughnessy Street, Port Coquitlam, BC V3C 2A8

**What requires a permit:**
- Structural changes (wall removal, beam installation)
- Plumbing relocation (new drain location, additional fixture)
- Electrical panel upgrade or rewiring
- Secondary suite creation or legalization

**Permit processing time:** 2–4 weeks (structural/electrical); cosmetic work (paint, flooring, fixture same-location swap) requires no permit.

