- [Cabinet Refinishing Cost Vancouver](/en/guides/cabinet-refinishing-cost-vancouver/) | [Cabinet Refinishing Vancouver](/en/services/cabinet/vancouver/) — from $4K for refinishing' WHERE id = '60a5c078-e9f8-47ce-b6d1-84eb94244a6c' AND content_en = '<h2>Introduction</h2><p>In the bustling city of [Vancouver](/en/areas/vancouver/), where modern living meets natural beauty, homeowners are increasingly seeking personalized spaces that reflect their unique tastes. Our recent project, a custom [whole house renovation](/en/guides/whole-house-renovation-cost-vancouver/), exemplifies this trend. Located in the heart of Vancouver, this renovation project was designed to transform a condo into a bespoke living space with tailored wall lines, custom paint colors, and striking design elements.</p><h2>Project Overview</h2><p>This comprehensive renovation involved a complete overhaul of a Vancouver condo. The project focused on space design, light optimization, and painting, with a budget of $25,000 to $27,000 and a timeline of 2-3 weeks. Our team worked diligently to create a cohesive design that included accent walls and optimized lighting, enhancing the overall aesthetic with custom tinted paint and decorative wall panels.</p><h2>Challenges</h2><p>One of the main challenges we faced was coordinating the custom paint colors to match the client''s vision while adhering to a tight timeline. This required meticulous planning and communication to ensure that every detail was executed flawlessly.</p><h2>Our Solution</h2><p>To address the challenge of custom paint coordination, we conducted thorough consultations with the client. We provided samples for approval, ensuring that the colors aligned perfectly with the client''s expectations. This proactive approach not only guaranteed client satisfaction but also facilitated the timely completion of the project.</p><h2>Before & After</h2><div><h3>Living Room Transformation</h3><img src="https://pub-b88db8c50fd64a9a87f60a4486a4a488.r2.dev/uploads/admin/social-ready-before-1-mmtwonp4.jpg" alt="Custom [Whole House Renovation](/en/services/whole-house/) in Vancouver - Before Renovation 1"><img src="https://pub-b88db8c50fd64a9a87f60a4486a4a488.r2.dev/uploads/admin/social-ready-after-1-mmtwonp5.jpg" alt="Custom Whole House Renovation in Vancouver - After Renovation 1"></div><div><h3>Kitchen Revamp</h3><img src="https://pub-b88db8c50fd64a9a87f60a4486a4a488.r2.dev/uploads/admin/social-ready-before-2-mmtwonp5.jpg" alt="Custom Whole House Renovation in Vancouver - Before Renovation 2"><img src="https://pub-b88db8c50fd64a9a87f60a4486a4a488.r2.dev/uploads/admin/social-ready-after-2-mmtwonp5.jpg" alt="Custom Whole House Renovation in Vancouver - After Renovation 2"></div><div><h3>Final Touches</h3><img src="https://pub-b88db8c50fd64a9a87f60a4486a4a488.r2.dev/uploads/admin/social-ready-after-3-mmtwonp5.jpg" alt="Custom Whole House Renovation in Vancouver - After Renovation 3"><img src="https://pub-b88db8c50fd64a9a87f60a4486a4a488.r2.dev/uploads/admin/social-ready-after-4-mmtwonp5.jpg" alt="Custom Whole House Renovation in Vancouver - After Renovation 4"><img src="https://pub-b88db8c50fd64a9a87f60a4486a4a488.r2.dev/uploads/admin/social-ready-after-5-mmtwonp6.jpg" alt="Custom Whole House Renovation in Vancouver - After Renovation 5"><img src="https://pub-b88db8c50fd64a9a87f60a4486a4a488.r2.dev/uploads/admin/social-ready-after-6-mmtwonp6.jpg" alt="Custom Whole House Renovation in Vancouver - After Renovation 6"><img src="https://pub-b88db8c50fd64a9a87f60a4486a4a488.r2.dev/uploads/admin/social-ready-hero-copy-mmtwonp6.jpg" alt="Custom Whole House Renovation in Vancouver - Renovation Photo 7"></div><h2>Results & Key Takeaways</h2><p>The final outcome of this renovation was a stunning, personalized living space that exceeded the client''s expectations. The use of custom paint and decorative elements created a unique atmosphere that was both modern and inviting. The client expressed immense satisfaction with the results, particularly appreciating the attention to detail and the seamless execution of their vision. This project highlights the importance of clear communication and meticulous planning in achieving a successful renovation.</p>



Whole-house renovations are also an ideal time to incorporate [accessible bathroom features](/services/accessible-bathroom/) such as grab bars, step-in showers, and wider doorways — future-proofing the home for years to come.


Many Metro Vancouver homeowners are also upgrading to a [heat pump HVAC system](/services/heat-pump-hvac/) during major renovations — providing both heating and cooling in one energy-efficient unit, and qualifying for BC Hydro rebates.


When renovation projects add new appliances, EV charging stations, or smart home systems, a [critical load panel upgrade](/services/critical-load-panel/) is often needed to safely handle the increased electrical load.


If you live in a strata property (condo or townhouse), review BC''s [strata renovation rules](/blog/strata-renovation-rules-vancouver/) before starting work — many projects require strata council approval and must follow specific noise, hour, and contractor requirements.
## Frequently Asked Questions

### What is a custom whole house renovation in Vancouver and how does it differ from a standard renovation?
A custom whole house renovation in Vancouver is designed around the specific tastes, lifestyle, and functional requirements of the homeowner rather than following a standard template. Custom finishes — bespoke cabinetry, imported tile, custom millwork, tailored lighting design — distinguish this approach from a standard renovation using off-the-shelf products. Custom renovations in Vancouver condos and homes typically cost 30–60% more than equivalent standard renovations but deliver a uniquely personal result that cannot be replicated in a developer-grade space.

### How much does a custom condo renovation cost in Vancouver?
A custom condo renovation in Vancouver (kitchen, bathrooms, custom millwork, and full finishes) typically costs $80,000–$180,000+ depending on unit size and finish level. A 700–900 sqft condo with custom kitchen cabinetry, renovated bathrooms, custom built-ins, and premium flooring typically runs $80,000–$130,000. High-end projects with European appliances, custom stone, and designer fixtures in 1,000+ sqft units can exceed $200,000.

### How long does a custom Vancouver condo renovation take?
Custom condo renovations in Vancouver typically take 12–20 weeks of active construction, longer than standard renovations because custom materials have longer lead times (custom cabinets 8–12 weeks, imported tile 4–8 weeks) and custom work requires more on-site fitting and adjustment. Strata approval and building permit processing add 4–8 weeks before construction begins. Plan for 5–7 months total from design approval to move-in for a fully custom renovation.

### Do custom renovations in Vancouver require different permits than standard renovations?
No — custom renovations require the same permit types as standard renovations. Any plumbing changes, electrical modifications, or structural alterations require City of Vancouver building permits regardless of finish level. The difference is that custom projects often involve more complex scope that requires engineering documentation for structural changes or MEP (mechanical, electrical, plumbing) redesign, which adds professional fees. Older Metro Vancouver homes may also need our [Poly-B Pipe Replacement](/en/services/poly-b-replacement/) service to eliminate unsafe plastic piping. A custom renovation company should manage permit applications as part of the project scope.

### What should I prioritize in a custom Vancouver condo renovation?
Prioritize investments visible to daily use and to buyers: custom kitchen cabinetry (the single most-impactful custom element in any home), primary bathroom as a spa-quality retreat, flooring throughout (sets the tone for the entire space), and lighting design (layered lighting transforms how spaces feel). Custom millwork — built-in wardrobes, integrated media walls, bespoke bookshelves — adds livability without structural complexity and photographs exceptionally well for resale.

