UPDATE blog_posts SET content_en = '<h2>Introduction</h2><p>In the heart of [Coquitlam](/en/areas/coquitlam/), a vibrant city in the Vancouver, BC area, Reno Stars embarked on an exciting [whole house renovation](/en/services/whole-house/) project. This endeavor aimed to breathe new life into a dated interior, transforming it into a stylish and modern living space.</p><h2>Project Overview</h2><p>The Coquitlam whole house renovation focused on updating the interiors with a fresh and modern look. The project encompassed floor renovations, complete wall painting, and retaining a feature wallpaper in the bedrooms. The overall budget for this transformation was between $24,000 and $26,000, with an estimated duration of 6 to 8 weeks.</p><h3>Standard [Bathroom Renovation](/en/services/bathroom/) with Shower Conversion</h3><p>One of the key areas of focus was the standard bathroom renovation, which involved converting an old bathtub into a sleek, modern shower. This transformation featured gray tiles, silver fixtures, and a frameless glass door, enhancing the bathroom''s contemporary appeal.</p><h2>Challenges</h2><p>During the bathroom renovation, a significant challenge was ensuring proper drainage and waterproofing for the new shower setup. This was crucial to prevent future water damage and maintain the integrity of the renovation.</p><h2>Our Solution</h2><p>To address the drainage and waterproofing challenge, our team implemented a comprehensive waterproofing system. We also adjusted the plumbing to accommodate the new shower layout, ensuring a seamless and efficient water flow.</p><h2>Before & After</h2><div><h3>Bathroom Transformation</h3><p>Before the renovation, the bathroom featured an outdated bathtub and lacked modern aesthetics.</p><img src="https://pub-b88db8c50fd64a9a87f60a4486a4a488.r2.dev/uploads/admin/social-ready-before-1-mmpcovju.jpg" alt="Standard Bathroom Renovation with Shower Conversion - Before Renovation 1"><img src="https://pub-b88db8c50fd64a9a87f60a4486a4a488.r2.dev/uploads/admin/social-ready-after-1-mmpcovju.jpg" alt="Coquitlam Home Renovation 2026: Whole-House Project Case Study - After Renovation 1"><p>After the renovation, the bathroom was transformed with a sleek shower, gray tiles, and modern fixtures.</p></div><div><p>Another angle of the bathroom before the renovation.</p><img src="https://pub-b88db8c50fd64a9a87f60a4486a4a488.r2.dev/uploads/admin/social-ready-before-2-mmpcovju.jpg" alt="Standard Bathroom Renovation with Shower Conversion - Before Renovation 2"><img src="https://pub-b88db8c50fd64a9a87f60a4486a4a488.r2.dev/uploads/admin/social-ready-after-2-mmpcowvl.jpg" alt="Coquitlam Home Renovation 2026: Whole-House Project Case Study - After Renovation 2"></div><div><p>Final view of the bathroom transformation showcasing the frameless glass door.</p><img src="https://pub-b88db8c50fd64a9a87f60a4486a4a488.r2.dev/uploads/admin/social-ready-before-3-mmpcowvm.jpg" alt="Standard Bathroom Renovation with Shower Conversion - Before Renovation 3"><img src="https://pub-b88db8c50fd64a9a87f60a4486a4a488.r2.dev/uploads/admin/social-ready-after-3-mmpcowvm.jpg" alt="Coquitlam Home Renovation 2026: Whole-House Project Case Study - After Renovation 3"></div><h2>Results & Key Takeaways</h2><p>The whole house renovation in Coquitlam was a resounding success. The stylish updates throughout the home, particularly in the bathroom, exceeded the client''s expectations. The project was completed within budget and on schedule, showcasing our commitment to quality and customer satisfaction. This case study highlights the importance of meticulous planning and execution in achieving a modern and functional living space.</p>



Whole-house renovations are also an ideal time to incorporate [accessible bathroom features](/services/accessible-bathroom/) such as grab bars, step-in showers, and wider doorways — future-proofing the home for years to come.


Many Metro Vancouver homeowners are also upgrading to a [heat pump HVAC system](/services/heat-pump-hvac/) during major renovations — providing both heating and cooling in one energy-efficient unit, and qualifying for BC Hydro rebates.
## Frequently Asked Questions

### How much does a [whole house renovation cost](/en/guides/whole-house-renovation-cost-vancouver/) in Coquitlam, BC?
A whole house renovation in Coquitlam aimed at modernizing a dated interior typically costs $35,000–$85,000 depending on scope. A comprehensive cosmetic update — flooring, paint, kitchen refresh, bathroom updates, and lighting — runs $35,000–$60,000. Full gut renovations with structural changes and new kitchen and bathrooms range $80,000–$150,000. Coquitlam renovation costs are comparable to Metro Vancouver averages, with the City''s permit process typically running 2–4 weeks for residential projects.

### What renovation work delivers the most impact in a Coquitlam home?
In Coquitlam homes (often 1980s–2000s builds), the highest-impact renovations are: flooring replacement (removing dated carpet and laminate for LVP or engineered hardwood transforms the entire home), kitchen cabinet refresh or replacement, bathroom updates (new tile, vanity, frameless glass), fresh neutral paint throughout, and lighting modernization (replacing old fixtures with LED pot lights and pendant lighting). These changes address the most buyer-visible and owner-lived-in spaces simultaneously.

### How long does a Coquitlam whole house renovation take?
A comprehensive Coquitlam home renovation at cosmetic-to-light scope typically takes 6–12 weeks of active construction. Full renovations requiring permits (kitchen plumbing changes, electrical panel work, bathroom rough-in) run 14–20 weeks including City of Coquitlam permit processing (typically 2–4 weeks). Our [Critical Load Panel Installation](/en/services/critical-load-panel/) service upgrades your home electrical capacity for modern renovation demands. Older Metro Vancouver homes may also need our [Poly-B Pipe Replacement](/en/services/poly-b-replacement/) service to eliminate unsafe plastic piping. For strata properties in Coquitlam, add 3–5 weeks for Alteration Approval before construction begins. See our guide to [BC Strata Renovation Rules](/en/blog/strata-renovation-rules-vancouver/) for Metro Vancouver homeowners.

### Why do homeowners in Coquitlam renovate before selling?
Coquitlam''s active real estate market — particularly for detached homes in the $1.2M–$1.8M range — strongly rewards move-in-ready presentation. Unrenovated Coquitlam homes with dated interiors typically sell for $30,000–$80,000 below renovated equivalents and sit on the market longer. For expert [Pre-Sale Renovation Advice](/en/services/realtor/) before listing, speak with our renovation team. A $40,000–$60,000 renovation that modernizes the interior can shorten days-on-market by 30–60% and position the home to receive multiple competing offers.

### What makes Reno Stars the right choice for a Coquitlam renovation?
Reno Stars has completed multiple renovation projects in Coquitlam, with direct experience in the City''s permit process and local trade network. We offer fixed-price contracts with a dedicated project manager, coordinating all trades under one scope. Our Coquitlam clients consistently rate completed projects 4.9/5 for quality, timeline adherence, and communication throughout the renovation process.

