### What was the specific scope of this West Vancouver budget condo renovation?
This West Vancouver condo renovation was completed within a $26,000–$28,000 budget over 3–4 weeks, focusing on the kitchen and bathroom as the highest-impact spaces. The scope included: cabinet painting (refreshing existing cabinets rather than replacing), countertop replacement, and new flooring installed throughout the entire condo. This scope sequence — cabinets first, then countertops to match, then floors to tie it all together — ensures a cohesive new look without the cost of full cabinet replacement. West Vancouver condos carry premium resale values, meaning a well-executed $26,000–$28,000 refresh delivers a strong return relative to renovation investment.


