## Strata Approval: City of North Vancouver vs. District of North Vancouver

North Vancouver is split between **City of North Vancouver** (CNV — Lonsdale core, Central Lonsdale, Lower Lonsdale) and **District of North Vancouver** (DNV — Lynn Valley, Capilano, Deep Cove, Edgemont Village). Both have different strata bylaws and building permit offices.

**City of North Vancouver** — Building Permits: 141 West 14th Street, North Vancouver BC V7M 1H9; cnv.org/building-development; Permit fees: $250–$1,500 for interior renovations. Permit required for plumbing changes, electrical panel upgrades, wall removals.

**District of North Vancouver** — Building Permits: 355 West Queens Road, North Vancouver BC V7N 4N5; dnv.org/development; Permit fees: $300–$1,800. DNV Heritage Inventory areas (Deep Cove, Capilano) may require additional heritage review.

**Strata Corporation Approval** — Before any permit, you need written approval from your strata council (typically within 30 days). Requirements include: written renovation plan with materials list; contractor liability insurance ($2M minimum); IIC-50 sound attenuation compliance for hard flooring; no work outside Monday–Friday, 8AM–6PM; damage deposit $500–$2,000 (refundable). Submit your renovation request at least 4–6 weeks before your planned start date.

## The Lonsdale Corridor: Renovation Priorities by Building Type

**Concrete high-rises (15+ storeys)** — Lonsdale Avenue, Esplanade: Excellent soundproofing; 2005–2018 construction with reasonable base finishes. Focus: kitchen upgrade, bathroom refresh, flooring replacement.

**Wood-frame mid-rises (4–6 storeys)** — Central Lonsdale, 14th Street corridor: Older construction (1995–2010) with dated finishes. Check for Poly-B plumbing: budget $4,000–$8,000 for replacement. Higher priority for full kitchen reno and electrical panel review.

**Townhouse strata complexes** — Lynn Valley, Capilano, Edgemont: Larger square footage (1,200–2,000 sq ft). Renovation budgets typically $80,000–$180,000. Basement entrances and structural changes need DNV permit.

## North Vancouver Rental Market: Post-Renovation Returns

North Vancouver''s rental vacancy rate consistently stays below 1.5%.

