## West Vancouver Neighbourhood Pre-Sale Strategy

### Ambleside (Below Keith Road, $2M–$5M)
The most accessible West Van neighbourhood and the entry point for most buyers. Our [Accessible Bathroom Renovation](/en/services/accessible-bathroom/) service specialises in safety upgrades and accessibility modifications. Mix of 1950s–1980s ranchers and newer infill construction. Pre-sale focus: full kitchen renovation, bathroom updates, fresh neutral paint, hardwood or LVP floors. Walkability to village amenities and waterfront is a strong selling point — clean, modern presentation matters here.

Budget: $60,000–$120,000 for a complete pre-sale package.

### Dundarave ($2.5M–$6M)
Village atmosphere with boutique shops and waterfront. Older character homes benefit from high-quality renovation more than modern infill. Pre-sale focus: preserve heritage character while modernizing kitchen and bathrooms. Original millwork and hardwood should be restored, not replaced.

### British Properties ($3M–$15M)
The most prestigious address in West Vancouver. Large lots, view homes, established trees. Buyers here are the most sophisticated and least tolerant of compromise. Pre-sale renovation must be comprehensive: kitchen, all bathrooms, mechanical systems, outdoor spaces. Budget $200,000–$500,000 for trophy British Properties pre-sale packages.

### Caulfield and Cypress Park ($2.5M–$7M)
Newer construction (1980s–2000s) with a mix of families and couples. Less renovation required than older Ambleside/Dundarave stock, but kitchens and master baths still benefit from updates. Outdoor spaces and views are strong selling points to develop.

### Horseshoe Bay ($1.5M–$4M)
More relaxed market; buyers are drawn to the ferry village atmosphere and connection to Squamish. Pre-sale investments should be moderate — focus on condition (fresh paint, updated kitchen fixtures, clean landscaping) rather than luxury finishes.

