## Choosing a Contractor in Port Moody

Verification checklist:
1. **BC Housing Licence**: Check bchousing.org — mandatory for contracts over $10,000
2. **WorkSafeBC**: Download clearance letter at worksafebc.com/clearanceletter — confirm it''s current
3. **Liability Insurance**: Minimum $2M commercial general liability
4. **Tri-Cities experience**: Ask for references from Port Moody, Coquitlam, or Port Coquitlam projects — contractors familiar with local permit offices and strata norms save time
5. **Written contract**: Detailed scope, itemised materials, payment schedule (max 10% deposit), 2-year craftsmanship warranty

Reno Stars serves Port Moody and the full Tri-Cities area with English/Mandarin bilingual project management. We handle all permits, coordinate all trades, and provide a 2-year warranty on all work.

## Frequently Asked Questions

**How much does a typical bathroom renovation cost in Port Moody?**
A mid-range full renovation (complete gut, new tile, walk-in shower, quartz vanity) runs $25,000–$42,000 in Port Moody in 2026. Premium ensuites with freestanding tub and frameless glass run $43,000–$60,000+.

**Do I need a permit to renovate my bathroom in Port Moody?**
You need a permit for any plumbing relocation, new electrical circuits, or structural changes. Older Metro Vancouver homes may also need our [Poly-B Pipe Replacement](/en/services/poly-b-replacement/) service to eliminate unsafe plastic piping. Like-for-like fixture replacement and tile work on existing surfaces typically don''t require a permit. Apply online at portmoody.ca/building.

**How long does a permit take in Port Moody?**
The District of Port Moody targets 10–15 business days for standard residential renovation permits. Budget 3–4 weeks total (application prep + review + approval) when planning your project timeline.

**Can I renovate my strata bathroom in Heritage Mountain?**
Yes, but you need strata council approval before work begins. Submit your renovation request with your contractor''s insurance and WorkSafeBC documents. Most Heritage Mountain strata councils also require dust control plans and noise hour restrictions.

**What''s the best ROI bathroom upgrade in Port Moody?**
Converting a tub/shower combo to a walk-in shower with large-format tile and frameless glass delivers the highest perceived value per dollar spent in Port Moody''s market — typically returning 70–85% of cost in property value, plus significantly improving liveability for the occupants. Our [Accessible Bathroom Renovation](/en/services/accessible-bathroom/) service specialises in safety upgrades and accessibility modifications.


**What is the total timeline for a Port Moody bathroom renovation project?**
A Port Moody bathroom renovation runs 7–14 weeks total from demo to final inspection: demolition and rough-in (2–4 days), tile and waterproofing (1–2 weeks), vanity and fixture installation (1–2 days), glass enclosure (1 day after tile cure), and final inspection (1–2 days). City of Port Moody permit processing adds 2–3 weeks upfront. For strata properties (Heritage Mountain, Rocky Point), add 4–8 weeks for strata council approval before starting any work. See our guide to [BC Strata Renovation Rules](/en/blog/strata-renovation-rules-vancouver/) for Metro Vancouver homeowners.


