## Frequently Asked Questions

### How much does a bathroom renovation with glass doors cost in Maple Ridge, BC?
A modern bathroom renovation in Maple Ridge featuring frameless glass shower enclosures typically costs $14,000–$28,000 depending on size and scope. Frameless glass shower doors or enclosures add $1,800–$4,000 compared to framed glass or a shower curtain alternative. At this investment level in Maple Ridge, the renovation includes demolition, new flooring, wall tile in the shower area, new vanity and fixtures, lighting update, and the glass enclosure — a comprehensive transformation from a dated bathroom to a modern oasis.

### Why are frameless glass shower doors recommended for Maple Ridge bathroom renovations?
Frameless glass enclosures are the standard finish for upper-mid to high-quality bathroom renovations in Metro Vancouver because they: eliminate the mould-prone metal channels of framed shower doors, create a visually larger shower space, photograph dramatically better for resale listings, and require less maintenance over time. In Maple Ridge''s growing market, where homes are attracting buyers relocating from higher-cost areas of Metro Vancouver, renovation quality expectations have risen significantly since 2022.

### What does a complete bathroom renovation scope include in Maple Ridge?
A complete Maple Ridge bathroom renovation typically includes: full demolition to the studs, new cement board or waterproof membrane tile backer, floor tile and wall tile in the shower zone, new bathtub or shower base, frameless glass enclosure, new vanity with countertop and undermount sink, toilet replacement, lighting fixtures and exhaust fan, baseboards, and all fixtures (faucets, shower valve, towel bars, mirror). Permit required if any plumbing is moved or new circuits added.

### How long does a bathroom renovation take in Maple Ridge?
A complete single bathroom renovation in Maple Ridge typically takes 3–5 weeks of active construction: 3–4 days demo, 3–4 days plumbing and electrical rough-in (inspected), 5–7 days tile installation and curing, 3–4 days vanity, glass, and fixture installation, and 1–2 days cleanup and final inspection. Ridge Meadows permit processing for residential bathroom renovations runs 2–3 weeks. Total timeline from contract signing to a completed bathroom: approximately 6–9 weeks.

### Is renovating a bathroom in Maple Ridge a good investment?
Maple Ridge''s real estate market has grown significantly, with detached home prices in the $900,000–$1.3M range attracting buyers from higher-cost Metro Vancouver cities. In this market, a well-renovated bathroom adds $15,000–$30,000 to perceived home value for a $15,000–$25,000 renovation investment — strong ROI in a market where buyers increasingly expect updated finishes. For expert [Pre-Sale Renovation Advice](/en/services/realtor/) before listing, speak with our renovation team. Updated bathrooms also reduce inspection objections and buyer requests for price adjustments at offer time.

