The "IKEA is half the price" headline holds at the small-kitchen end if you compare base IKEA against high-end custom. As the kitchen scales, the absolute dollar gap narrows because IKEA''s per-foot cost stays similar while custom''s economies of scale kick in.

A real example from our portfolio: see how a [budget-friendly Coquitlam kitchen renovation](/en/blog/budget-friendly-kitchen-renovation-in-coquitlam) used IKEA-tier cabinets to land under $35,000 total renovation cost, vs. a [Langley waterfall island kitchen](/en/blog/langley-kitchen-renovation-waterfall-island) that used semi-custom to hit $28,000–$30,000 in cabinets alone with a more demanding layout.

