UPDATE blog_posts SET content_en = '<h2>Introduction</h2><p>In the bustling area of Metrotown, [Burnaby](/en/areas/burnaby/), a toy store was in need of a refreshing transformation. Reno Stars took on the challenge to revitalize this commercial space, ensuring it met both aesthetic and regulatory standards.</p><h2>Project Overview</h2><p>This [commercial reno](/en/guides/commercial-renovation-cost-vancouver/)vation project involved a comprehensive overhaul of a toy store located in Metrotown, Burnaby. The scope of work included wall modifications, complete painting, and the installation of laminate flooring. With a budget of $23,000 to $25,000, the project was slated to be completed within 2 to 3 weeks.</p><h2>Challenges</h2><p>One of the primary challenges was ensuring compliance with government regulations throughout the renovation process. This required meticulous planning and coordination with local authorities to ensure all modifications adhered to the necessary standards.</p><h2>Our Solution</h2><p>To address the regulatory challenges, our team worked closely with local government officials. We ensured that every aspect of the renovation, from wall modifications to flooring installation, complied with the required standards, thereby avoiding any potential delays or issues.</p><h2>Before & After</h2><p>Although we don''t have the ''before'' images, the transformation is evident in the ''after'' images. The toy store now boasts a fresh and inviting look, thanks to the new paint and laminate flooring.</p><img src="https://pub-b88db8c50fd64a9a87f60a4486a4a488.r2.dev/uploads/admin/social-ready-after-1-mmwscdzk.jpg" alt="Toy Store Renovation in Metrotown, Burnaby - After 1"><img src="https://pub-b88db8c50fd64a9a87f60a4486a4a488.r2.dev/uploads/admin/social-ready-after-2-mmwscdzl.jpg" alt="Toy Store Renovation in Metrotown, Burnaby - After 2"><img src="https://pub-b88db8c50fd64a9a87f60a4486a4a488.r2.dev/uploads/admin/social-ready-after-3-mmwscdzl.jpg" alt="Toy Store Renovation in Metrotown, Burnaby - After 3"><img src="https://pub-b88db8c50fd64a9a87f60a4486a4a488.r2.dev/uploads/admin/social-ready-after-4-mmwscdzl.jpg" alt="Toy Store Renovation in Metrotown, Burnaby - After 4"><img src="https://pub-b88db8c50fd64a9a87f60a4486a4a488.r2.dev/uploads/admin/social-ready-after-5-mmwscdzm.jpg" alt="Toy Store Renovation in Metrotown, Burnaby - After 5"><img src="https://pub-b88db8c50fd64a9a87f60a4486a4a488.r2.dev/uploads/admin/social-ready-after-6-mmwscdzm.jpg" alt="Toy Store Renovation in Metrotown, Burnaby - After 6"><img src="https://pub-b88db8c50fd64a9a87f60a4486a4a488.r2.dev/uploads/admin/social-ready-after-7-mmwscdzm.jpg" alt="Toy Store Renovation in Metrotown, Burnaby - After 7"><img src="https://pub-b88db8c50fd64a9a87f60a4486a4a488.r2.dev/uploads/admin/social-ready-after-8-mmwscdzn.jpg" alt="Toy Store Renovation in Metrotown, Burnaby - After 8"><h2>Results & Key Takeaways</h2><p>The renovation was completed on time and within budget, resulting in a vibrant and compliant commercial space. The client was extremely satisfied with the transformation, noting the improved aesthetic appeal and functionality of the store. This project highlights the importance of adhering to regulations while delivering high-quality results.</p>

## Frequently Asked Questions

### What does a commercial retail renovation at Metrotown in Burnaby typically include?
A retail renovation at Metrotown, Burnaby''s major retail centre, typically includes: custom fixture and display systems designed to the tenant''s brand, lighting optimized for product display (typically 3,000–4,000K LED with high CRI), flooring appropriate for high-foot-traffic retail (commercial LVT or polished concrete), updated signage (subject to Metrotown landlord approval and Burnaby sign permit), and code-compliant electrical for display lighting and POS systems. All work must meet BC Building Code requirements for commercial occupancy and pass City of Burnaby inspections.

### How much does a retail store renovation in Metrotown cost?
A commercial retail renovation in a Metrotown-area store typically costs $60,000–$150,000 for a 1,000–2,500 sqft unit depending on the extent of fixture work, electrical, and finishes required. Toy and children''s retail stores require durable, easily-cleanable surfaces and robust display fixtures built to handle active interaction. Landlord-mandated tenant improvement standards at Metrotown can add requirements (base building tie-ins, specific finish categories) that increase costs compared to standalone retail locations.

### What permits are required for a retail store renovation in Burnaby?
A City of Burnaby building permit is required for any retail renovation involving construction, partition changes, electrical, plumbing, or HVAC work. Older Metro Vancouver homes may also need our [Poly-B Pipe Replacement](/en/services/poly-b-replacement/) service to eliminate unsafe plastic piping. For food-adjacent retail or premises with specific occupancy requirements, additional Fraser Health or BC Fire Commissioner approvals may apply. Permit applications for commercial projects in Burnaby typically process in 3–6 weeks. Tenant improvements also require landlord approval and often involve coordination with the Metrotown property management team.

### How does Reno Stars manage [commercial renovation](/en/services/commercial/) while respecting retail trading hours?
Commercial retail renovations in active shopping centres like Metrotown typically cannot proceed during mall trading hours. Reno Stars coordinates renovation work to take place during off-hours (typically 10 p.m.–8 a.m.) and during mall closure periods. All materials, equipment, and debris are managed to maintain clear public corridors per BC Fire Code requirements. Noise-generating work (demolition, concrete cutting) is scheduled during the lowest-traffic overnight windows with advance notice to mall management.

### What design considerations are unique to children''s retail store renovation?
Children''s retail spaces in Metro Vancouver require: robust, impact-resistant surfaces rated for high-volume interaction, rounded or protected corners on all fixtures per BC safety standards, interactive display configurations at child height (45–90cm), bright, high-CRI lighting (85+ CRI) to make product colours accurate and appealing, and non-toxic finishes throughout. All materials must meet applicable Canadian toy and children''s product safety standards. Flooring should be slip-resistant per BC Building Code commercial requirements.

