When renovation projects add new appliances, EV charging stations, or smart home systems, a [critical load panel upgrade](/services/critical-load-panel/) is often needed to safely handle the increased electrical load.
## Frequently Asked Questions

### Q: How much does a bathroom renovation cost in White Rock?
A: Budget $14,000-$18,000 for a standard 5x8 refresh, $20,000-$28,000 for mid-range, $28,000-$35,000 for a premium master ensuite, and $42,000+ for an ocean-view luxury curbless bathroom. Nearby Surrey projects we have finished run $14K-$32K; Delta and West Van reference projects push to $42K-$60K for larger scopes.

### Q: Do I need a permit for a bathroom renovation in White Rock?
A: Yes for anything that relocates plumbing, changes drains, or moves walls. Fixture-swap-only refreshes (same location vanity, tub, toilet) usually don''t need one, but the City of White Rock can still require a plumbing permit if you are replacing the toilet flange or moving the drain stack. Older Metro Vancouver homes may also need our [Poly-B Pipe Replacement](/en/services/poly-b-replacement/) service to eliminate unsafe plastic piping.

### Q: How long does a White Rock bathroom renovation take?
A: 2-3 weeks on site for a standard gut-to-re-tile, 4-6 weeks for a larger master or dual-bathroom scope, and 8-11 weeks for luxury ocean-view projects with structural changes. Add 1-2 weeks for permits and 2-4 weeks for strata approval if you are in a beach-front condo.

### Q: What materials hold up best in White Rock''s coastal climate?
A: Porcelain tile (not ceramic), epoxy grout in wet areas, solid-brass fixtures with PVD finish, marine-grade 316 stainless for anything exposed to salt air, plywood vanity boxes, and a humidity-sensing ventilation fan rated at least 80 CFM. Consider our [Heat Pump Installation Vancouver](/en/services/heat-pump-hvac/) service to upgrade heating and cooling with modern energy-efficient systems. Avoid MDF cabinet boxes, zinc-alloy hardware, and unbranded chrome tapware. Our [cabinet refinishing](/en/services/cabinet/) service can transform your cabinets without full replacement.

### Q: Can I renovate a bathroom in an ocean-view White Rock condo?
A: Yes, but most strata corporations require written approval before work starts, a licensed plumber, $1M liability insurance naming the strata, weekday-only work hours (typically 9-5), and sometimes noise-restriction bylaws. See our guide to [BC Strata Renovation Rules](/hi/blog/strata-renovation-rules-vancouver/) for Metro Vancouver homeowners. Budget 2-4 weeks for approvals on top of the normal permit and construction timeline.

### Q: Do you serve South Surrey neighborhoods like Morgan Creek, Grandview Heights, and Ocean Park?
A: Yes, Reno Stars serves all of White Rock and South Surrey including Morgan Creek, Grandview Heights, Ocean Park, Crescent Beach, Sunnyside, and Pacific Douglas. We also work north into Cloverdale, Fleetwood, and Guildford.


