Pure painting and refacing don''t require permits in Maple Ridge. Full replacement that moves plumbing (e.g., relocating the sink) or electrical (new circuit for a range) requires a plumbing and/or electrical permit — we pull them for you. Older Metro Vancouver homes may also need our [Poly-B Pipe Replacement](/en/services/poly-b-replacement/) service to eliminate unsafe plastic piping. See our [BC renovation permits guide](/en/blog/renovation-permits-bc-guide/) | [Vancouver Renovation Cost Guide 2026](/en/blog/renovation-cost-vancouver-2026-complete-guide/) | [How to Choose a Contractor](/en/blog/how-to-choose-renovation-contractor-vancouver/) | [Pre-Sale Renovation Advice](/en/services/realtor/) | [Renovation Timeline Guide](/en/blog/renovation-timeline-how-long-does-each-project-take/).

### Do you serve Pitt Meadows and Mission?
Yes — we cover Pitt Meadows and Mission at Maple Ridge pricing. There''s no travel surcharge within the Fraser Valley.


### How much does cabinet painting or refacing cost in Maple Ridge in 2026?

Maple Ridge cabinet refinishing costs in 2026: Professional painting (all boxes, doors, and drawer fronts, new hardware): $4,000–$8,000. Cabinet refacing (new doors, drawer fronts, new veneer on boxes): $8,000–$15,000. Full cabinet replacement: $18,000–$45,000+. Painting timeline for a Maple Ridge kitchen: 3–5 business days on-site, plus 1 week cure time before heavy use. Maple Ridge homeowners planning a spring listing should book cabinet painting in February or March to ensure the project is complete and fully cured before listing photographs.
