## What Cabinet Refinishing Includes

Cabinet refinishing (used interchangeably with resurfacing or refacing in most Lower Mainland quotes) keeps your existing boxes and updates the visible parts: doors, drawer fronts, end panels, hardware, and sometimes face frames. In Maple Ridge, most homes built between 1995 and 2010 have solid cabinet boxes made from plywood or MDF — the boxes are fine; it''s the doors and hardware that look 25 years old.

## [Cabinet Refinishing Costs](/en/guides/cabinet-refinishing-cost-vancouver/) in Maple Ridge (2026)

| Option | Cost Range | Timeline | What''s Included |
|-' || '-' || '-|-' || '-' || '-|-' || '-' || '-|-' || '-' || '-|
| **Cabinet Painting** | $4,000–$8,000 | 5–7 days | Spray-finished doors + boxes with bonding primer and two finish coats. Hardware reuse or basic upgrade. |
| **Door Refacing** | $8,000–$15,000 | 1–2 weeks | Factory-finished shaker or slab doors + drawer fronts on existing boxes, matching end panels, soft-close hinges, new handles. |
| **Full Replacement** | $18,000–$45,000+ | 3–6 weeks | All cabinets removed and replaced. New boxes, doors, soft-close hinges, and interior organizers. |

Add **$3,000–$8,000** if you''re replacing the countertop during the same project. The counter has to come off for refacing anyway — bundling saves the cost of a second removal and reinstall.

Real Fraser Valley kitchen costs from our recent projects:

- **Langley white shaker kitchen** — $20,000–$23,000 over 4–5 weeks (full replacement, stock shaker doors, quartz counter). See the [Langley kitchen project](/en/projects/modern-kitchen-renovation-langley/).
- **Langley waterfall-island kitchen** — $28,000–$30,000 over 4–6 weeks (full replacement, semi-custom cabinets, waterfall quartz island).
- **Coquitlam budget-friendly kitchen** — $25,000–$27,000 over 5–6 weeks (full replacement, mid-range cabinets).
- **Surrey custom kitchen** — $35,000–$38,000 over 4–5 weeks (semi-custom, shaker doors, full soft-close).

Browse more [kitchen renovation projects](/en/services/kitchen/) for finishes and layouts.

## Which Option Fits Your Maple Ridge Kitchen?

**Choose painting if:**
- Boxes and doors are solid wood or MDF (paint will peel off thermofoil or melamine — we test on-site before quoting)
- You like the door style but not the colour
- Budget is under $8,000
- Timeline is tight (under 2 weeks)

**Choose refacing if:**
- Boxes are solid but doors are worn, chipped, or dated
- You want a different door profile (raised-panel oak → shaker, cathedral arch → slab)
- You want soft-close hinges and new hardware included
- Budget is $8,000–$15,000

**Choose full replacement if:**
- Boxes are swelling, water-damaged, or particle board at the base
- You''re changing layout (adding an island, opening to the living room, removing a peninsula) — common in 1990s Albion and Cottonwood homes
- You''re already doing a full kitchen reno (counters, backsplash, electrical, plumbing)
- You want manufacturer warranties on cabinets

## Common Maple Ridge Cabinet Types (and What Works for Each)

**1995–2005 Silver Valley and West Maple Ridge homes** typically have oak or maple raised-panel doors with plywood boxes. Both paint and reface well. Painting to crisp white or deep navy is the single biggest visual upgrade.

**2005–2015 Albion and Cottonwood homes** typically have cherry or espresso shaker doors. Painting light requires heavy primer blocking (dark stain bleeds through cheap primer). Refacing to bright shaker is often cleaner.

**Pre-1995 central Maple Ridge homes** often have original oak with dated cathedral-arch doors and laminate countertops. Refacing + new counter is usually the right call — the jump to modern shaker transforms the space and leaves the plumbing and electrical untouched.

**Strata townhomes** around Haney and downtown Maple Ridge: refacing or painting is almost always easier to get strata approval than full replacement, since there''s no plumbing or electrical work involved. Our [Critical Load Panel Installation](/en/services/critical-load-panel/) service upgrades your home electrical capacity for modern renovation demands. See our guide to [BC Strata Renovation Rules](/en/blog/strata-renovation-rules-vancouver/) for Metro Vancouver homeowners.

## Our Maple Ridge Cabinet Refinishing Process

1. **Free in-home consultation** — measure every cabinet, test door material, check box condition, discuss colour and door style. Fixed written quote within 2–3 business days.
2. **Material selection** — visit our [Richmond showroom](/en/areas/richmond/) for door samples, colour chips, and hardware. Confirm profile, finish, hinges, and handles in writing.
3. **Site prep** — floors, appliances, and open-plan living space covered with heavy plastic and rosin paper. Open-concept kitchens get a temporary dust barrier.
4. **Dismantle** — doors, drawer fronts, hinges, and hardware removed and labeled for reinstall.
5. **Painting**: deep-clean, sand, bonding primer, two finish coats sprayed in our shop. Doors returned and reinstalled in 5–7 days. **Refacing**: factory-finished doors and drawer fronts arrive, end panels cut on-site, soft-close hinges and handles installed.
6. **Walk-through** — on-the-spot touch-ups and written warranty.

We also do cabinet-only projects in Maple Ridge as part of [bathroom renovations](/en/services/bathroom/) — vanity resurfacing, linen cabinet paint, powder room vanity swaps. Real project: see our [Maple Ridge bathroom with custom glass door](/en/projects/).

## ROI — Does Cabinet Refinishing Make Sense in Maple Ridge?

Maple Ridge benchmark home prices are $1.1M–$1.4M for detached homes in Silver Valley and Albion (2026). A **$6,000 painted kitchen** typically returns 60–80% of cost at sale in photos and showings alone — the kitchen is the top MLS photo after the exterior. A **$12,000 refaced kitchen** returns less on paper but is often the difference between a stale listing and a quick sale.

If you''re planning to stay 5+ years, **full replacement** makes sense: you''ll enjoy soft-close drawers, full-height pantry organization, and a modern layout for a decade. Under 2 years, stick with painting or refacing — full replacement won''t pay back in that window.

See our full [pre-sale renovation guide](/en/blog/pre-sale-renovation-vancouver-what-to-fix-before-listing/) for the complete pre-listing playbook and [renovate-vs-move decision guide](/en/blog/renovate-vs-move-vancouver-2026/) for longer-term stays.



