Converting a tub to a walk-in shower in a Richmond townhouse is the right choice when the bathroom is primarily used by adults who prefer shower bathing. However, retaining at least one tub in the home is recommended for resale purposes — Metro Vancouver real estate agents consistently advise that homes with no tub are harder to sell to buyers with young children. If your Richmond townhouse has two full bathrooms, converting one to a shower-only while retaining a tub in the other is the ideal balance.

### How long does a two-bathroom and powder room renovation take in Richmond?
Active construction for a dual bathroom plus powder room renovation in a Richmond townhouse takes 4–7 weeks: demo week one, plumbing and electrical rough-in (inspected) weeks two to three, tile and glass installation weeks three to five, and fixtures and finishing week six to seven. Strata council approval (required for any plumbing or flooring change) adds 3–5 weeks before construction begins. Total project timeline: approximately 2–3 months from contract signing to completed renovation.

### Why choose Reno Stars for a multi-bathroom renovation in Richmond?
Reno Stars has completed numerous multi-bathroom renovation projects throughout Richmond, with familiarity in Richmond''s strata requirements and permit process. Our single-contract approach covers all trade coordination — plumbing, electrical, tile, glass, carpentry, and finishing — with a dedicated project manager tracking every phase. Older Metro Vancouver homes may also need our [Poly-B Pipe Replacement](/en/services/poly-b-replacement/) service to eliminate unsafe plastic piping. Fixed-contract pricing means your budget is confirmed before construction begins, with no surprise change orders for standard scope items. Richmond clients rate our completed bathroom projects 4.9/5.

Related cost guide: [Bathroom Renovation Cost Vancouver 2026](/en/guides/bathroom-renovation-cost-vancouver/)

