## Frequently Asked Questions

### How much does it cost to renovate 3 bathrooms in a Delta townhouse?
A three-bathroom renovation in a Delta townhouse (including a half bath or powder room) typically costs $38,000–$70,000 at mid-range finishes. A main bathroom with shower and tub, a kids'' bathroom with shower only, and an ensuite each have distinct plumbing and layout requirements. Multi-bathroom projects often achieve cost efficiencies when tile orders, plumbing fixtures, and trade scheduling are coordinated across all bathrooms simultaneously — the per-bathroom cost drops by 10–20% compared to phasing bathrooms separately.

### Why renovate all bathrooms at once versus doing them one at a time in Delta?
Renovating all bathrooms simultaneously in a Delta townhouse maximizes efficiency and minimizes total project cost. Trade scheduling — plumbing rough-in, electrical, tile, glass installation — can be batched across all bathrooms, reducing mobilization costs. Material orders (tile, fixtures) can be coordinated for consistent style and potential bulk pricing. The disruption period is compressed: one 5–8 week renovation is less disruptive than three separate 2–3 week renovations spread across multiple years.

### What bathroom configuration works best for a Delta family townhouse?
The most functional multi-bathroom layout for Delta families includes: a main bathroom with both shower and tub (essential for young children), a secondary bathroom configured as shower-only (efficient for older children or guests), and a master ensuite with walk-in shower and upgraded fixtures. Our [Accessible Bathroom Renovation](/en/services/accessible-bathroom/) service specialises in safety upgrades and accessibility modifications. Powder rooms on main floors benefit from an elevated design with statement mirror and vessel sink — a relatively low-cost improvement that makes a strong impression on guests and buyers.

### How does a multi-bathroom renovation affect Delta townhouse resale value?
Updated bathrooms consistently rank among the highest-ROI renovations in Delta townhouses. A complete three-[bathroom renovation cost](/en/guides/bathroom-renovation-cost-vancouver/)ing $40,000–$65,000 typically adds $50,000–$90,000 in perceived resale value in Delta''s current market, particularly when the existing bathrooms are original 1980s–1990s finishes. Modern tile, frameless glass, and contemporary fixtures signal to buyers that the home is well-maintained and move-in-ready — Delta''s active family housing market rewards this presentation.

### What should I know about Delta strata and permit requirements for a bathroom renovation?
Delta requires a building permit for any bathroom renovation involving plumbing changes (new or relocated rough-in) or electrical alterations. Older Metro Vancouver homes may also need our [Poly-B Pipe Replacement](/en/services/poly-b-replacement/) service to eliminate unsafe plastic piping. For townhouses, the strata council must also approve the alteration before construction begins. Submit the strata application and permit application in parallel — both take 3–6 weeks. Your contractor should pull the building permit directly and provide the strata with a scope of work, contractor insurance, and WorkSafeBC compliance documentation.

