UPDATE blog_posts SET content_en = '<h2>Introduction</h2><p>Located in the picturesque area of [West Vancouver](/en/areas/west-vancouver/), this [whole-house renovation](/en/services/whole-house/) project was a transformative journey for the homeowners. The primary focus was on converting a single bathroom into two functional spaces, enhancing both utility and aesthetics. This case study explores the challenges and solutions involved in this remarkable renovation.</p><h2>Project Overview</h2><p>The scope of this renovation was extensive, involving the transformation of one bathroom into two distinct spaces. The project featured full wall tiling, custom wood grain cabinets, fresh paint, and new crown molding. Stylish materials such as white and gray patterned tiles, white quartz countertops, and LED mirrors were used to create a modern and inviting atmosphere. The overall budget for this project was between $57,000 and $60,000, and it was completed over a span of 9 to 11 weeks.</p><h2>Challenges</h2><p>The main challenge of this project was efficiently dividing the existing bathroom space while ensuring that both new bathrooms were functional and aesthetically pleasing. The limited space required careful planning and execution to meet the client''s needs and design preferences.</p><h2>Our Solution</h2><p>To address the challenges, our team meticulously planned the layout to maximize space utilization. High-quality materials were selected to ensure durability and style. Custom wood grain cabinets provided ample storage, while full wall tiles and LED mirrors enhanced the modern look. The use of white quartz countertops added a touch of elegance, ensuring that both bathrooms were not only functional but also visually appealing.</p><h2>Before & After</h2><div><img src="https://pub-b88db8c50fd64a9a87f60a4486a4a488.r2.dev/uploads/admin/social-ready-before-1-mmo6vyvh.jpg" alt="Transforming One Bathroom into Two in West Vancouver - Before Renovation 1"><img src="https://pub-b88db8c50fd64a9a87f60a4486a4a488.r2.dev/uploads/admin/social-ready-after-2-mmo6vyvk.jpg" alt="Whole House Renovation in West Vancouver - After Renovation 1"></div><p>The transformation from a single bathroom to two was remarkable. The before image shows the limited space that was creatively reimagined into two stylish and functional bathrooms.</p><h2>Results & Key Takeaways</h2><p>The renovation was a resounding success, with both bathrooms meeting the client''s expectations in terms of functionality and design. The use of modern materials and thoughtful layout planning resulted in a space that is both practical and elegant. The client expressed immense satisfaction with the outcome, appreciating the seamless blend of style and utility.</p>

<h2>Planning a similar West Vancouver bathroom?</h2>
<p>For full pricing breakdowns, BPP HOA notes, coastal-climate material guidance, and timeline expectations across all West Vancouver bathroom types, see our complete <a href="/en/blog/bathroom-renovations-west-vancouver-2026/">West Vancouver bathroom renovation guide for 2026</a>. See our guide to [BC Strata Renovation Rules](/en/blog/strata-renovation-rules-vancouver/) for Metro Vancouver homeowners.</p>



For homeowners planning for the future or needing improved mobility, our [accessible bathroom renovations](/services/accessible-bathroom/) service includes grab bars, walk-in showers, wider doorways, and slip-resistant flooring.


When renovation projects add new appliances, EV charging stations, or smart home systems, a [critical load panel upgrade](/services/critical-load-panel/) is often needed to safely handle the increased electrical load.
## Frequently Asked Questions

### How much does it cost to convert one bathroom into two in West Vancouver?
Converting a single bathroom into two separate functional spaces in a West Vancouver home typically costs $25,000–$50,000 depending on the existing plumbing configuration and how the space is divided. The conversion requires adding a new drain and supply rough-in for the second bathroom, new walls, separate ventilation for each space, and finishing each bathroom independently. West Vancouver homes often have premium construction quality that constrains where new walls can be placed, requiring careful structural assessment before design.

### What are the main challenges of splitting one bathroom into two in West Vancouver?
The primary challenges in West Vancouver bathroom splits are: (1) existing plumbing location — new drains must connect to the existing stack, and the distance limits where fixtures can be placed in each new bathroom; (2) ceiling height and mechanical clearances — West Vancouver homes often have specific mechanical runs above the bathroom that limit flexibility; (3) ventilation — BC Building Code requires independent exhaust ventilation for each bathroom, requiring new duct routes; and (4) permit requirements — structural changes and new plumbing require City of West Vancouver building permits (typically 3–5 weeks). Older Metro Vancouver homes may also need our [Poly-B Pipe Replacement](/en/services/poly-b-replacement/) service to eliminate unsafe plastic piping. Consider our [Heat Pump Installation Vancouver](/en/services/heat-pump-hvac/) service to upgrade heating and cooling with modern energy-efficient systems.

### How does splitting a bathroom into two affect home value in West Vancouver? For expert [Pre-Sale Renovation Advice](/en/services/realtor/) before listing, speak with our renovation team.
Converting one bathroom to two in a West Vancouver home typically adds more value than it costs in the $2M–$4M+ West Vancouver detached home market. Buyers in this segment expect multiple bathrooms proportionate to the home''s size — a 4-bedroom home with one full bathroom is a significant functional limitation. Adding a second bathroom removes this objection, broadens buyer appeal, and can add $50,000–$120,000 in perceived value depending on execution quality and the home''s overall specification level.

### Is whole house renovation in West Vancouver subject to different rules than Vancouver proper?
Yes. West Vancouver is a distinct municipality with its own Building and Planning department. Permits are issued by the District of West Vancouver, not the City of Vancouver. West Vancouver has specific design guidelines for exterior changes and Heritage designations in some areas. Renovation contractors working in West Vancouver should be familiar with the District''s specific permit application process, heritage overlay requirements, and inspection protocols. The permit process in West Vancouver typically takes 3–6 weeks for residential renovations.

### What makes a whole house renovation in West Vancouver different from other Metro Vancouver cities?
West Vancouver renovations typically operate at higher finish expectations than the Metro Vancouver average, reflecting the community''s premium property values ($2M–$6M+ for detached homes). Clients expect premium materials, high-precision execution, and professional project management. Renovation companies working in West Vancouver must source higher-end finishes, manage suppliers with premium products, and demonstrate a portfolio of completed projects at the appropriate quality level. Project management intensity is also higher due to client expectations and complex site logistics in mountainside properties.

Related cost guide: [Bathroom Renovation Cost Vancouver 2026](/en/guides/bathroom-renovation-cost-vancouver/)

