### What materials and finishes were used in this West Vancouver bathroom renovation?
This West Vancouver bathroom renovation featured full wall tiling, custom wood grain cabinets, fresh paint, and new crown molding — a combination that creates a warm, contemporary bathroom with character. The tile selection used white and gray patterned tiles, which add visual interest without committing to a heavily trend-driven look. White quartz countertops and LED mirrors completed the design. The total project budget was $57,000–$60,000. Custom wood grain cabinetry paired with white and gray patterned tile is particularly effective for West Vancouver bathrooms, creating a high-end look that feels designed rather than stock-renovated.


