## Frequently Asked Questions

### How much does a restaurant renovation cost in Vancouver?

Restaurant renovation costs in Metro Vancouver range from $50,000 for a cosmetic refresh to $500,000+ for a full buildout. A front-of-house refresh (new flooring, paint, lighting, seating) runs $50,000–$120,000. A mid-range full restaurant renovation with new kitchen equipment, hood ventilation, and FOH design runs $150,000–$300,000. A ground-up restaurant buildout in a raw commercial shell runs $250,000–$600,000+. Reno Stars real-project data: Metrotown casual dining buildout $280,000, Burnaby café renovation $143,000, Richmond bubble tea franchise buildout $165,000. Per-sqft costs: $200–$600/sqft for full restaurant renovations in Metro Vancouver.

### What permits do I need for a restaurant renovation in Vancouver?

A Vancouver restaurant renovation typically requires: (1) **Building permit** — for any structural, mechanical, or layout changes; (2) **Plumbing permit** — for kitchen sinks, dishwashers, grease traps, hand sinks; (3) **Electrical permit** — for hood fans, commercial equipment circuits, new panel capacity; (4) **Mechanical permit** — for Type 1 or 2 commercial exhaust hood and HVAC changes; (5) **Health permit** — from Vancouver Coastal Health or Fraser Health (inspects the completed kitchen before opening); (6) **Business licence** — renewed or updated with new address/use. The most common delay: ventilation system approval and grease trap sizing, which requires a mechanical engineer''s stamp in the City of Vancouver.

### How long does a restaurant renovation take in Vancouver?

A Metro Vancouver restaurant renovation timeline: permit submission (4–10 weeks), construction (6–12 weeks for full renovation), health inspection and final permits (1–3 weeks). Total from lease signing to open: 3–6 months for a mid-scope renovation; 6–12 months for a full buildout from a raw shell. Landlord coordination, liquor licence applications (8–16 weeks if new), and health authority inspections are the most variable elements. Reno Stars has completed 15+ commercial restaurant and café projects — we provide an integrated Gantt chart covering all permit and inspection milestones.

### What is the cost of commercial kitchen equipment installation in Vancouver?

Commercial kitchen equipment installation costs vary significantly by equipment type. Budget ranges for Metro Vancouver in 2026: commercial range ($8,000–$35,000 supply + $1,500–$4,000 install), commercial hood system ($6,000–$25,000 including makeup air), walk-in cooler ($18,000–$45,000 for 8×10 to 10×12 units), commercial dishwasher ($8,000–$25,000), grease trap ($3,000–$9,000), and ventilation/makeup air ($8,000–$30,000). Total commercial kitchen equipment budget for a 20-seat casual dining restaurant in Vancouver: $60,000–$140,000. Equipment procurement is often on the critical path — popular items have 8–16 week lead times from Canadian suppliers.

### Do I need a Type 1 or Type 2 hood for my Vancouver restaurant?

A Type 1 (grease-rated) commercial exhaust hood is required for any cooking equipment that produces grease-laden vapours — ranges, griddles, fryers, charbroilers. A Type 2 hood is for heat and moisture only (ovens, steam tables, dishwashers). In Vancouver''s City building code, all Type 1 hoods must include a fire suppression system (Ansul or equivalent), makeup air supply, and must meet NFPA 96 clearances. Grease duct runs must be single-wall welded steel or UL-listed duct. The most common compliance failure during restaurant renovation inspections in Vancouver: inadequate makeup air CFM for the hood size.

