## Room-by-Room Renovation Priorities for White Rock Homes

### Kitchen
White Rock buyers consistently prioritize kitchens. Open-plan kitchen-to-ocean-view-living-room layouts are particularly valued — removing a wall between kitchen and living room to frame the view is one of the highest-ROI changes in White Rock renovations. Budget $15,000–$35,000 for structural wall removal and beam installation, on top of kitchen renovation costs.

**White Rock kitchen renovation budget**: $45,000–$95,000 for a comprehensive renovation.

### Primary Bathroom
Luxury finishes perform especially well in White Rock due to the buyer demographic. Freestanding soaking tubs, frameless glass walk-in showers, and double vanities are near-standard expectations for homes in the $1. Our [Accessible Bathroom Renovation](/en/services/accessible-bathroom/) service specialises in safety upgrades and accessibility modifications.5M+ range.

**White Rock primary bathroom budget**: $28,000–$65,000.

### Flooring
Wide-plank engineered hardwood or natural stone tile throughout main floor is standard for White Rock renovations targeting the premium market. Typical cost: $18,000–$35,000 for full main floor replacement.

### Exterior and Deck
White Rock''s ocean climate accelerates wood decay. Composite decking ($15,000–$35,000) and durable exterior cladding ($20,000–$50,000) are recommended investments that significantly improve curb appeal and reduce long-term maintenance.

## Pre-Sale Renovation Strategy for White Rock

If you''re renovating specifically to sell, focus investment on areas with highest buyer visibility and emotional impact:

1. **Kitchen modernization**: New countertops, updated cabinet hardware, fresh backsplash — even a $20,000–$35,000 cosmetic kitchen refresh can yield $50,000–$80,000 in additional sale proceeds in the White Rock market
2. **Primary bathroom update**: Fresh tile, new vanity, updated fixtures — $15,000–$25,000 investment with strong visible impact
3. **Flooring**: Replace worn carpet throughout with LVP or hardwood — $10,000–$20,000 that removes one of the most common buyer objections
4. **Fresh paint throughout**: Neutral, warm tones — $5,000–$10,000 that makes every room photograph better and feel larger
5. **Curb appeal**: Landscaping refresh and exterior paint — $8,000–$18,000 for that critical first impression

A well-executed pre-sale renovation package in White Rock ($55,000–$90,000) typically returns $120,000–$175,000 in additional sale proceeds, based on recent comparable transactions.



Metro Vancouver homeowners increasingly include a [heat pump HVAC upgrade](/services/heat-pump-hvac/) in their renovation plans — these systems provide efficient heating and cooling year-round, and qualify for BC Hydro and CleanBC rebate programs.


If you live in a strata property (condo or townhouse), review BC''s [strata renovation rules](/blog/strata-renovation-rules-vancouver/) before starting work — many projects require strata council approval and must follow specific noise, hour, and contractor requirements.
## Frequently Asked Questions

**Do White Rock and Surrey have the same permit requirements?**
No. White Rock is an independent municipality. All building permits must be obtained from the City of White Rock (15322 Buena Vista Avenue), not from the City of Surrey. This is a common and costly mistake — starting work under a Surrey permit in White Rock is illegal.

**How long does a whole-home renovation take in White Rock?**
A comprehensive whole-home renovation (kitchen, bathrooms, flooring, painting) typically takes 10–18 weeks from permit approval to completion. Add 4–8 weeks for permit processing, giving a total project timeline of 14–26 weeks.

**Do I need to move out during renovation?**
For full whole-home renovations, most homeowners in White Rock vacate for 8–14 weeks. Some phased approaches allow partial occupancy, but complete vacating typically allows faster completion and reduces dust/noise impact on your household.

**What is the best renovation ROI in White Rock?**
Kitchen renovation, primary bathroom update, and flooring replacement consistently provide the strongest ROI in White Rock. Pre-sale renovations targeting these areas routinely return 150–200% of invested capital at time of sale.

**Does White Rock have specific regulations for hillside properties?**
Yes. Properties with slopes exceeding 15% grade may require a geotechnical engineering report before the City of White Rock issues a building permit for structural work. This is particularly relevant for additions, deck installations, and basement underpinning.

**How much does a whole-home renovation cost in White Rock in 2026?**
White Rock whole-home renovation costs: Cosmetic whole-home (flooring, paint, fixtures): $25,000–$60,000. Kitchen + bathrooms renovation: $60,000–$130,000. Full interior renovation (all rooms, layout changes): $120,000–$220,000. Whole-home gut renovation with additions: $200,000–$400,000+. White Rock''s hillside properties — particularly in the Marine Drive area with ocean views — tend to run 15–25% above standard Metro Vancouver renovation costs for equivalent scope due to access logistics, premium finish expectations, and coastal material requirements.



