UPDATE blog_posts SET content_en = '<h2>Introduction</h2><p>In the bustling industrial area of [Burnaby](/en/areas/burnaby/), BC, a commercial warehouse sought to enhance its entrance with a renovation project focused on the main door. This case study explores how Reno Stars successfully transformed the warehouse entrance, ensuring both aesthetic appeal and functionality.</p><h2>Project Overview</h2><p>The project involved a comprehensive renovation of a commercial warehouse door. Our team focused on repainting and drywall repairs to improve the entrance''s appearance and functionality. The project was completed within a budget of $8,000 and took less than a week, showcasing our efficiency and commitment to quality.</p><h2>Challenges</h2><p>The primary challenge was to meet commercial standards for the door renovation while minimizing disruption to the warehouse''s daily operations. This required careful planning and execution to ensure the project was completed swiftly and effectively.</p><h2>Our Solution</h2><p>To address these challenges, we scheduled the renovation during off-peak hours, allowing the warehouse to maintain its operations with minimal interference. Our team used efficient techniques and high-quality materials to ensure the renovation met all commercial standards.</p><h2>Before & After</h2><div><img src="https://pub-b88db8c50fd64a9a87f60a4486a4a488.r2.dev/uploads/admin/social-ready-after-1-mmo3msew.jpg" alt="Warehouse Door Renovation in Burnaby - After Renovation 1"><img src="https://pub-b88db8c50fd64a9a87f60a4486a4a488.r2.dev/uploads/admin/social-ready-after-2-mmo3msew.jpg" alt="Warehouse Door Renovation in Burnaby - After Renovation 2"><img src="https://pub-b88db8c50fd64a9a87f60a4486a4a488.r2.dev/uploads/admin/social-ready-after-3-mmo3msew.jpg" alt="Warehouse Door Renovation in Burnaby - After Renovation 3"><img src="https://pub-b88db8c50fd64a9a87f60a4486a4a488.r2.dev/uploads/admin/social-ready-after-4-mmo3msew.jpg" alt="Warehouse Door Renovation in Burnaby - After Renovation 4"><img src="https://pub-b88db8c50fd64a9a87f60a4486a4a488.r2.dev/uploads/admin/social-ready-after-5-mmo3msew.jpg" alt="Warehouse Door Renovation in Burnaby - After Renovation 5"><img src="https://pub-b88db8c50fd64a9a87f60a4486a4a488.r2.dev/uploads/admin/social-ready-after-6-mmo3msex.jpg" alt="Warehouse Door Renovation in Burnaby - After Renovation 6"></div><h2>Results & Key Takeaways</h2><p>The renovation was a resounding success, enhancing the warehouse''s entrance both visually and functionally. The client expressed high satisfaction with the minimal disruption to their operations and the quality of the work. This project highlights Reno Stars'' ability to deliver top-notch [commercial reno](/en/guides/commercial-renovation-cost-vancouver/)vations in the Vancouver, BC area.</p>

## Frequently Asked Questions

### How much does a commercial warehouse door renovation cost in Burnaby?
A commercial warehouse entrance door renovation in Burnaby — including new door unit, hardware, weatherstripping, and any associated framing or electrical for automatic operation — typically costs $8,000–$25,000 depending on door size, type, and automation requirements. Large industrial roll-up or sectional doors with automated openers cost more; man-doors and storefront glass entrances at the lower end. BC Building Code compliance for commercial egress and accessibility adds requirements that must be factored into the design.

### What [commercial renovation](/en/services/commercial/) permits are required for a Burnaby warehouse door?
Any structural modification to a commercial building''s entrance — including replacing a door with a different size or type, adding an automatic door operator that requires new electrical, or modifying the door frame opening — requires a City of Burnaby building permit. If the change affects the building''s fire egress path, Fire Code compliance documentation is also required. Burnaby commercial permit processing for this type of project typically takes 3–5 weeks. A renovation contractor experienced in Burnaby commercial permits is essential.

### What are the key considerations for a commercial warehouse entrance renovation?
Warehouse entrance renovations must balance four requirements: (1) security — the door and hardware must meet commercial security standards for the industrial context; (2) functionality — the door must accommodate the operational requirements, including forklift clearance heights if applicable, delivery traffic, and employee access; (3) safety — BC Building Code egress requirements must be met for the occupancy type; and (4) aesthetics — the entrance impression matters for clients and employees visiting the facility. All four factors should be addressed in the design brief before contractor selection.

### How does a renovated warehouse entrance benefit a Burnaby commercial business?
A renovated warehouse entrance improves both operational efficiency and business image. Functionally, a well-designed commercial entrance reduces energy loss (better weatherstripping and insulation in new door units), improves security (modern hardware and potentially automated access control), and accommodates high-frequency use without maintenance issues. From an image perspective, a professional entrance signals operational competence to suppliers, clients, and employees — meaningful for any Burnaby industrial business that receives visitors at the facility.

### How long does a commercial warehouse door renovation project take?
A commercial warehouse entrance door renovation in Burnaby typically takes 3–6 weeks from contract to completion: 2–3 weeks for permit processing, 1–2 weeks for door fabrication and hardware procurement (standard commercial door units are stock; custom sizes take longer), and 1–3 days for installation. Electrical for automatic door operators adds a licensed electrician visit (1–2 days) coordinated with the main installation. Planning around the warehouse''s operational schedule to minimize access disruption is standard practice for commercial renovation projects.

### Can a commercial renovation be done without disrupting warehouse operations in Burnaby?
Yes — minimizing operational disruption is a core planning requirement for commercial renovations in Burnaby''s industrial areas. The approach used in this project was scheduling active renovation work during off-peak hours, allowing the warehouse to maintain its daily operations with minimal interference throughout the project. Well-organized commercial contractors sequence the work so that noisy or access-blocking phases occur outside business-critical windows — typically early mornings, evenings, or weekends. This coordination between the renovation contractor and the business operator is especially important for warehouse entrances, where access for deliveries and employees cannot be blocked during operating hours.


