UPDATE blog_posts SET content_en = '<h2>Introduction</h2><p>In the heart of [Richmond](/en/areas/richmond/), BC, a townhouse underwent a remarkable transformation that brought elegance and simplicity to its interiors. This renovation project focused on two bathrooms and a kitchen, featuring the installation of stylish arched doors and a complete repaint of the home.</p><h2>Project Overview</h2><p>The scope of this renovation included the complete overhaul of two bathrooms with the addition of elegant arched doors, a kitchen makeover with white shaker cabinets, and a stunning white quartz countertop. The project was completed within a budget of $60,000 - $63,000 over a duration of 7-9 weeks.</p><h3>Service Scope</h3><ul><li>Cabinet Installation</li><li>Countertop Replacement</li><li>Backsplash Tiling</li><li>Plumbing</li><li>Lighting</li></ul><h2>Challenges</h2><p>One of the main challenges was to seamlessly integrate the new arched doors with the existing design while maintaining functionality. This required careful planning and a keen eye for detail.</p><h2>Our Solution</h2><p>Our team addressed this challenge by meticulously planning the layout and selecting materials that complemented the overall aesthetic. This ensured that the new design was both beautiful and practical, enhancing the warmth and simplicity of the townhouse.</p><h2>Before & After</h2><div><img src="https://pub-b88db8c50fd64a9a87f60a4486a4a488.r2.dev/uploads/admin/social-ready-before-1-mmo1mbw1.jpg" alt="Two [Bathroom Renovation](/en/services/bathroom/) with Arched Doors - Before Renovation 1"><img src="https://pub-b88db8c50fd64a9a87f60a4486a4a488.r2.dev/uploads/admin/social-ready-after-1-mmo1mbw2.jpg" alt="Two Bathroom Renovation with Arched Doors in Richmond - After Renovation 1"></div><div><img src="https://pub-b88db8c50fd64a9a87f60a4486a4a488.r2.dev/uploads/admin/social-ready-before-2-mmo1mbw2.jpg" alt="Two Bathroom Renovation with Arched Doors - Before Renovation 2"><img src="https://pub-b88db8c50fd64a9a87f60a4486a4a488.r2.dev/uploads/admin/social-ready-after-2-mmo1mbw2.jpg" alt="Two Bathroom Renovation with Arched Doors in Richmond - After Renovation 2"></div><div><img src="https://pub-b88db8c50fd64a9a87f60a4486a4a488.r2.dev/uploads/admin/social-ready-before-3-mmo1mbw2.jpg" alt="Two Bathroom Renovation with Arched Doors - Before Renovation 3"><img src="https://pub-b88db8c50fd64a9a87f60a4486a4a488.r2.dev/uploads/admin/social-ready-after-3-mmo1mbw3.jpg" alt="Two Bathroom Renovation with Arched Doors in Richmond - After Renovation 3"></div><div><img src="https://pub-b88db8c50fd64a9a87f60a4486a4a488.r2.dev/uploads/admin/social-ready-before-4-mmo1mbw3.jpg" alt="Two Bathroom Renovation with Arched Doors - Before Renovation 4"><img src="https://pub-b88db8c50fd64a9a87f60a4486a4a488.r2.dev/uploads/admin/social-ready-after-4-mmo1mbw3.jpg" alt="Two Bathroom Renovation with Arched Doors in Richmond - After Renovation 4"></div><h2>Results & Key Takeaways</h2><p>The final outcome was a set of beautifully renovated bathrooms and a kitchen that exuded warmth and simplicity. The client was delighted with the seamless integration of the new features, particularly the arched doors, which added a touch of elegance to the home. This project highlights the importance of careful planning and material selection in achieving a harmonious design.</p>



For homeowners planning for the future or needing improved mobility, our [accessible bathroom renovations](/services/accessible-bathroom/) service includes grab bars, walk-in showers, wider doorways, and slip-resistant flooring.


Many Metro Vancouver homeowners also upgrade to a [heat pump HVAC system](/services/heat-pump-hvac/) during renovations — providing efficient year-round heating and cooling while qualifying for CleanBC rebates.


Renovations that add high-draw appliances or modern lighting often benefit from a [critical load panel upgrade](/services/critical-load-panel/) to ensure adequate electrical capacity and safety.


If you live in a strata property (condo or townhouse), review BC''s [strata renovation rules](/blog/strata-renovation-rules-vancouver/) before starting work — many projects require strata council approval and must follow specific noise, hour, and contractor requirements.
## Frequently Asked Questions

### What makes arched interior doors a distinctive renovation choice in Richmond?
Arched interior doors add architectural character to Richmond townhouses and condos that would otherwise have standard flat or square-top door frames. The arch detail photographs dramatically well and creates memorable visual interest in listing photos — a key advantage in Richmond''s competitive real estate market. Arched doors are most impactful when carried through consistently (bathroom doors, bedroom doors, or hallway entries) rather than applied to a single door, creating a cohesive design language throughout the home.

### How much does a two-bathroom renovation plus kitchen update cost in Richmond, BC?
A comprehensive renovation covering two bathrooms and a kitchen update in a Richmond townhouse typically costs $32,000–$60,000 at mid-range finishes. Two full bathroom renovations run $22,000–$38,000 combined; a kitchen update (new countertops, backsplash, and hardware without full cabinet replacement) adds $8,000–$15,000; a full home repaint adds $4,000–$8,000. Distinctive architectural elements like arched door installations add $2,000–$5,000 but provide outsized visual differentiation.

### Does a whole-home repaint as part of a renovation in Richmond add significant value?
Yes — professional interior repainting is one of the highest-ROI components of any renovation in Richmond''s condo and townhouse market. Fresh neutral paint (warm white or greige tones) eliminates dated colour choices, covers minor surface wear, and creates the clean slate that makes all other renovation elements look their best. A $4,000–$8,000 professional repaint of a Richmond townhouse consistently contributes to a stronger listing presentation and buyer perception of a well-maintained home.

### How long does a two-bathroom, kitchen, and repaint renovation take in Richmond?
This type of multi-scope renovation in Richmond typically takes 6–10 weeks of active construction. Bathroom work (the critical path for plumbing inspections) takes 3–5 weeks per bathroom when done sequentially; scheduling both bathrooms in overlapping phases reduces total time to 5–7 weeks. Older Metro Vancouver homes may also need our [Poly-B Pipe Replacement](/en/services/poly-b-replacement/) service to eliminate unsafe plastic piping. Kitchen updates and repainting can proceed in parallel with bathroom finishing work. Strata approval (required for Richmond townhouses) adds 3–5 weeks before construction can begin.

### Are arched doors appropriate for a Richmond townhouse renovation aimed at resale? For expert [Pre-Sale Renovation Advice](/en/services/realtor/) before listing, speak with our renovation team.
Arched doors are an increasingly popular and well-received design choice in Richmond''s townhouse market. They add architectural distinctiveness without the risk associated with more trend-dependent choices. When executed cleanly — consistent arch radius, properly cased frames, doors that swing and seal correctly — arched doors become a signature feature that listing agents can highlight. Richmond buyers in the $800K–$1.3M townhouse range respond well to thoughtful design details that signal quality craftsmanship.

