UPDATE blog_posts SET content_en = '<h2>Introduction</h2><p>Located in the beautiful city of [Delta](/en/areas/delta/), just outside Vancouver, BC, this renovation project showcases the transformation of two bathrooms in a townhouse. With a focus on modern elegance, the use of brushed gold fixtures and frameless glass doors creates a stunning aesthetic that elevates the home''s overall appeal.</p><h2>Project Overview</h2><p>This project involved a comprehensive renovation of two bathrooms. One bathroom was converted from a bathtub to a shower, while the other retained its bathtub. The design incorporated white tiles, brushed gold fixtures, and frameless glass doors, achieving a modern and elegant look. The renovation was completed within a budget of $40,000 - $43,000 over a period of 6-8 weeks.</p><h2>Challenges</h2><p>The primary challenge was to efficiently redesign the layout to accommodate a shower in one bathroom while ensuring the other bathroom remained functional with a bathtub. This required careful planning to maximize space and maintain a cohesive design across both bathrooms.</p><h2>Our Solution</h2><p>Our team addressed these challenges by meticulously planning the space and selecting materials that complemented both bathrooms. By using consistent design elements, such as the brushed gold fixtures and white tiles, we ensured a harmonious look. The installation of frameless glass doors added to the modern aesthetic, while careful plumbing and lighting adjustments enhanced functionality.</p><h2>Before & After</h2><div><img src="https://pub-b88db8c50fd64a9a87f60a4486a4a488.r2.dev/uploads/admin/social-ready-before-1-mmmnf6f5.jpg" alt="Two [Bathroom Renovation](/en/services/bathroom/) with Brushed Gold Fixtures - Before Renovation 1"><img src="https://pub-b88db8c50fd64a9a87f60a4486a4a488.r2.dev/uploads/admin/social-ready-after-1-mmmnf6f6.jpg" alt="Modern bathroom featuring a wooden vanity, large mirror, and sleek fixtures."></div><div><img src="https://pub-b88db8c50fd64a9a87f60a4486a4a488.r2.dev/uploads/admin/social-ready-before-2-mmmnf6rs.jpg" alt="Two Bathroom Renovation with Brushed Gold Fixtures - Before Renovation 2"><img src="https://pub-b88db8c50fd64a9a87f60a4486a4a488.r2.dev/uploads/admin/social-ready-after-2-mmmnf6rt.jpg" alt="Modern bathroom featuring a glass shower, freestanding tub, and sleek black fixtures."></div><div><img src="https://pub-b88db8c50fd64a9a87f60a4486a4a488.r2.dev/uploads/admin/social-ready-before-3-mmmnf6rt.jpg" alt="Two Bathroom Renovation with Brushed Gold Fixtures - Before Renovation 3"><img src="https://pub-b88db8c50fd64a9a87f60a4486a4a488.r2.dev/uploads/admin/social-ready-after-3-mmmnf71o.jpg" alt="Modern bathroom with wooden vanity, dual mirrors, and sleek fixtures."></div><div><img src="https://pub-b88db8c50fd64a9a87f60a4486a4a488.r2.dev/uploads/admin/social-ready-before-4-mmmnf71o.jpg" alt="Two Bathroom Renovation with Brushed Gold Fixtures - Before Renovation 4"><img src="https://pub-b88db8c50fd64a9a87f60a4486a4a488.r2.dev/uploads/admin/social-ready-after-4-mmmnf71p.jpg" alt="Modern bathroom featuring a wooden vanity, round mirror, and festive wreath decoration."></div><div><img src="https://pub-b88db8c50fd64a9a87f60a4486a4a488.r2.dev/uploads/admin/social-ready-before-5-mmmnf7dz.jpg" alt="Two Bathroom Renovation with Brushed Gold Fixtures - Before Renovation 5"><img src="https://pub-b88db8c50fd64a9a87f60a4486a4a488.r2.dev/uploads/admin/social-ready-after-5-mmmnf7dz.jpg" alt="Modern bathroom featuring a wooden vanity, white toilet, and stylish mirror with lighting."></div><h2>Results & Key Takeaways</h2><p>The renovation successfully transformed both bathrooms into modern, elegant spaces. The client was thrilled with the cohesive design and the functionality of each bathroom. The use of brushed gold fixtures and frameless glass doors not only enhanced the aesthetic appeal but also added value to the property. This project highlights the importance of thoughtful design and planning in achieving a successful renovation.</p>



Metro Vancouver homeowners increasingly include a [heat pump HVAC upgrade](/services/heat-pump-hvac/) in their renovation plans — these systems provide efficient heating and cooling year-round, and qualify for BC Hydro and CleanBC rebate programs.


When renovation projects add new appliances, EV charging stations, or smart home systems, a [critical load panel upgrade](/services/critical-load-panel/) is often needed to safely handle the increased electrical load.
## Frequently Asked Questions

### How much does a two-[bathroom renovation cost](/en/guides/bathroom-renovation-cost-vancouver/) in Delta, BC?
A dual bathroom renovation in a Delta townhouse typically costs $22,000–$45,000 for both bathrooms at mid-range finishes. This project — converting one bathroom from bathtub to shower with brushed gold fixtures and installing frameless glass doors in both — represents a mid-to-upper renovation scope. Converting a tub to a walk-in shower adds $3,000–$6,000 in plumbing modification costs but significantly increases usability and resale appeal in homes where the tub is not the primary bathing option.

### Are brushed gold fixtures a timeless choice for a bathroom renovation?
Brushed gold fixtures have moved from trend status into the classic renovation palette since approximately 2020 and remain a strong choice in 2026 for Metro Vancouver bathrooms. The key to longevity is restraint — brushed gold works best as an accent (faucets, shower hardware, towel bars, mirrors) against neutral tile and cabinetry, rather than as a dominant colour. Mixed metal combinations (brushed gold hardware with matte black drain covers) are a common and sophisticated approach in Vancouver renovation projects.

### How does converting a bathtub to a walk-in shower affect resale value in Delta?
In Delta townhouses targeting families, the primary bathroom typically benefits from retaining a tub for young children, while secondary or ensuite bathrooms are prime candidates for tub-to-shower conversion. Eliminating all tubs from a home is a resale risk; keeping at least one tub for the family bathroom is recommended by most Metro Vancouver real estate agents. A walk-in shower in a secondary bathroom adds usability and visual appeal without sacrificing the family-friendly feature. Our [Accessible Bathroom Renovation](/en/services/accessible-bathroom/) service specialises in safety upgrades and accessibility modifications.

### What makes frameless glass shower doors worth the premium in a Vancouver bathroom?
Frameless glass shower enclosures cost $1,500–$3,500 more than framed alternatives but offer significant advantages: easier cleaning (no metal channels to accumulate soap scum), larger perceived opening, and a clean modern aesthetic that photographs exceptionally well for resale listings. In Delta''s renovation market, frameless glass is the standard expectation for upper-mid to high-end bathroom renovations. The premium is reliably recouped at resale in the $1M+ Delta detached home price range.

### How long does a two-bathroom renovation take in a Delta townhouse?
A dual bathroom renovation in a Delta townhouse typically takes 5–8 weeks including strata approval and permit processing. Active construction takes 3–5 weeks: demo week one, rough-in plumbing and electrical (inspected) week two, tile and glass installation weeks three to four, and fixtures and finishing week five. Older Metro Vancouver homes may also need our [Poly-B Pipe Replacement](/en/services/poly-b-replacement/) service to eliminate unsafe plastic piping. Strata approval for the alteration adds 3–5 weeks before construction can begin. Plan for 2–3 months total from contract signing to completed bathrooms.

