Basement renovation costs in Port Coquitlam run $30,000–$110,000 depending on scope, consistent with broader Metro Vancouver pricing. A basic open-concept basement finish (framing, drywall, LVP flooring, pot lights, no bathroom): $30,000–$50,000. A full basement with bathroom, wet bar, and storage: $50,000–$75,000. A legal secondary suite with separate entrance, kitchen, bathroom, and 1-hour fire separation: $65,000–$110,000. Permit fees from the City of Port Coquitlam add $600–$1,500. Port Coquitlam has relatively faster permit processing (3–5 weeks for standard residential) compared to the City of Vancouver. Reno Stars provides [free quote](/en/contact/)s for Port Coquitlam basement projects within 24 hours.

### Does the City of Port Coquitlam allow secondary suites?

Yes — Port Coquitlam allows secondary suites in most single-family residential zones (RS zones). Requirements align with BC Building Code: 1-hour fire-rated separation (walls and ceiling to upper floor), minimum ceiling height of 6''5", dedicated electrical circuit, egress windows in bedrooms, and separate exterior entrance. As of 2026, the city also allows detached garden suites (ADUs) on most RS lots subject to setback requirements. Reno Stars has completed multiple legal suite conversions in Port Coquitlam and is familiar with the local building department''s inspection process and requirements.

### How long does a basement renovation take in Port Coquitlam?

A standard basement renovation in Port Coquitlam takes 8–14 weeks from permit approval to handover. Timeline: Port Coquitlam building permit processing (3–5 weeks), construction including framing, rough-ins, drywall, and finishing (6–10 weeks), final inspection (1–2 weeks). Legal suite projects take 12–18 weeks due to additional inspections (plumbing, electrical, insulation, framing, final). Reno Stars provides a project schedule and weekly progress updates via our client portal. We submit permit packages to Port Coquitlam on behalf of the client.

### What permits are needed for a basement renovation in Port Coquitlam?

Required permits for a basement renovation in Port Coquitlam: (1) **Building permit** — for all framing, insulation, drywall, and layout changes; (2) **Electrical permit** (ESA — Electrical Safety Authority) — for new circuits, panel additions, pot lights; (3) **Plumbing permit** — if adding a bathroom, wet bar, or laundry; (4) **Mechanical permit** — if adding [HVAC](/en/services/heat-pump-hvac/) or HRV connections. For secondary suites: all four permits are required plus a final suite registration with the City. Permit fees: $600–$1,400 for a typical $50,000–$80,000 basement renovation. Reno Stars coordinates all permit applications and arranges all required inspections.

### What should I look for when hiring a contractor for a Port Coquitlam basement renovation?

When hiring a basement renovation contractor in Port Coquitlam: verify their Consumer Protection BC license (rpsportal.consumerprotectionbc.ca), request a WCB clearance letter (worksafebc.com), ask for $2M+ CGL insurance certificate, check Google reviews and portfolio of local projects, confirm they pull permits (never work with a contractor who suggests skipping permits), and get 2–3 itemized written quotes. Be wary of contractors offering dramatically below-market prices — basement work involves electrical, plumbing, and structural work where cutting corners creates safety and resale risks. Older Metro Vancouver homes may also need our [Poly-B Pipe Replacement](/en/services/poly-b-replacement/) service to eliminate unsafe plastic piping. Reno Stars carries $5M CGL insurance, active WCB coverage, and references from completed Port Coquitlam projects.

