UPDATE blog_posts SET content_en = '<h2>Introduction</h2><p>In the bustling city of [Richmond](/en/areas/richmond/), BC, a townhouse has undergone a remarkable transformation. This [whole house renovation](/en/services/whole-house/) project by Reno Stars aimed to convert a traditional living space into a modern, inviting home. With a budget-friendly approach, the project included re-tiling the first floor, painting the entire home, and replacing light fixtures, creating a fresh and inviting atmosphere.</p><img src="https://pub-b88db8c50fd64a9a87f60a4486a4a488.r2.dev/uploads/admin/social-ready-hero-mmmrrp3p.png" alt="Richmond Whole House Renovation - Hero Image"><h2>Project Overview</h2><p>This comprehensive renovation project in Richmond was completed with a budget of $75,000 to $78,000 over a span of 7 to 9 weeks. The renovation encompassed two major areas: the bathrooms and the kitchen, each with its unique set of challenges and solutions.</p><h3>Area 1: Two [Bathroom Renovation](/en/services/bathroom/) with Custom Features</h3><p>The bathroom renovation involved a complete overhaul of two bathrooms. One bathroom was transformed from a bathtub to a shower, while the other underwent a full four-piece renovation featuring gray tiles and silver fixtures, complemented by custom frameless glass doors.</p><h3>Area 2: Modern [Kitchen Renovation](/en/services/kitchen/) | [Cabinet Refinishing](/en/services/cabinet/) | [Pre-Sale Renovation Advice](/en/services/realtor/) in [Burnaby](/en/areas/burnaby/)</h3><p>The kitchen renovation aimed to create a modern, family-friendly space. This involved repainting cabinets, replacing countertops with white quartz, and installing stylish gray-veined tiles.</p><h2>Challenges</h2><h3>Bathroom Renovation Challenges</h3><p>The main challenge was managing the renovation of two bathrooms simultaneously while minimizing disruption to the family''s daily routine.</p><h3>Kitchen Renovation Challenges</h3><p>Coordinating the color scheme to ensure a cohesive modern look while accommodating the family''s needs was a significant challenge.</p><h2>Our Solution</h2><h3>Bathroom Renovation Solution</h3><p>We implemented a phased approach to the renovation, allowing one bathroom to be completed before starting on the second, ensuring the family had access to essential facilities throughout the project.</p><h3>Kitchen Renovation Solution</h3><p>We addressed the color scheme challenge by selecting a neutral palette and modern materials that appeal to both adults and children, ensuring functionality and style.</p><h2>Before & After</h2><div><h3>Bathroom Renovation</h3><img src="https://pub-b88db8c50fd64a9a87f60a4486a4a488.r2.dev/uploads/admin/social-ready-before-1-mmmrrqgt.jpg" alt="Two Bathroom Renovation with Custom Features - Before Renovation 1"><img src="https://pub-b88db8c50fd64a9a87f60a4486a4a488.r2.dev/uploads/admin/social-ready-after-1-mmmrrqgu.jpg" alt="Modern bathroom featuring a glass shower, bathtub, and sleek gray tiles."><img src="https://pub-b88db8c50fd64a9a87f60a4486a4a488.r2.dev/uploads/admin/social-ready-before-2-mmmrrqq6.jpg" alt="Two Bathroom Renovation with Custom Features - Before Renovation 2"><img src="https://pub-b88db8c50fd64a9a87f60a4486a4a488.r2.dev/uploads/admin/social-ready-after-2-mmmrrqq7.jpg" alt="Modern bathroom featuring a glass shower, sleek vanity, and contemporary lighting."></div><div><h3>Kitchen Renovation</h3><img src="https://pub-b88db8c50fd64a9a87f60a4486a4a488.r2.dev/uploads/admin/social-ready-before-1-mmmrrrc7.jpg" alt="Modern Kitchen Renovation in Burnaby - Before Renovation 1"><img src="https://pub-b88db8c50fd64a9a87f60a4486a4a488.r2.dev/uploads/admin/social-ready-after-1-mmmrrrc8.jpg" alt="Modern kitchen featuring dark cabinetry and marble countertops with a sleek design."><img src="https://pub-b88db8c50fd64a9a87f60a4486a4a488.r2.dev/uploads/admin/social-ready-before-2-mmmrrrc8.jpg" alt="Modern Kitchen Renovation in Burnaby - Before Renovation 2"><img src="https://pub-b88db8c50fd64a9a87f60a4486a4a488.r2.dev/uploads/admin/social-ready-after-2-mmmrrrn6.jpg" alt="Bright, modern room with white walls, marble flooring, and plantation shutters."></div><h2>Results & Key Takeaways</h2><p>The Richmond whole house renovation was a resounding success. The transformation resulted in a modern, cohesive living space that met the family''s needs while staying within budget. The client expressed immense satisfaction with the results, praising the team''s professionalism and attention to detail. This project highlights the importance of strategic planning and execution in achieving a seamless renovation.</p>



Whole-house renovations are also an ideal time to incorporate [accessible bathroom features](/services/accessible-bathroom/) such as grab bars, step-in showers, and wider doorways — future-proofing the home for years to come.


Many Metro Vancouver homeowners are also upgrading to a [heat pump HVAC system](/services/heat-pump-hvac/) during major renovations — providing both heating and cooling in one energy-efficient unit, and qualifying for BC Hydro rebates.
## Frequently Asked Questions

### How much does a [whole house renovation cost](/en/guides/whole-house-renovation-cost-vancouver/) in Richmond, BC?
A whole house renovation in Richmond typically ranges from $25,000–$150,000+ depending on scope. A cosmetic refresh — flooring, paint, light fixtures, and hardware throughout — runs $20,000–$40,000 and delivers a high-impact transformation without structural changes. A comprehensive renovation including kitchen, bathrooms, and electrical updates ranges $80,000–$180,000. The project in this case study demonstrated that a budget of $25,000–$40,000 can produce a dramatically improved home when scope is well-defined and materials are pre-selected.

### How long does a whole house renovation take in Richmond?
A cosmetic whole house renovation in Richmond typically takes 4–8 weeks of active construction. Full renovations involving kitchen and bathroom remodels, electrical panel upgrades, and permit-required plumbing work run 14–22 weeks including Richmond City permit approval (typically 2–4 weeks, faster than City of Vancouver). Our [Critical Load Panel Installation](/en/services/critical-load-panel/) service upgrades your home electrical capacity for modern renovation demands. Townhouse renovations in Richmond must also account for strata approval timelines of 4–6 weeks before construction can begin.

### Do I need strata approval for a whole house renovation in a Richmond townhouse?
Yes — Richmond townhouse strata corporations require written Alteration Approval before any renovation involving shared systems, flooring (for noise transmission compliance), plumbing, or structural changes begins. Older Metro Vancouver homes may also need our [Poly-B Pipe Replacement](/en/services/poly-b-replacement/) service to eliminate unsafe plastic piping. The contractor must provide a scope of work, insurance certificates, and WorkSafeBC coverage. The approval process typically takes 2–6 weeks. A renovation company experienced in Richmond strata projects can prepare the application package and anticipate common council requirements.

### What trades are involved in a whole house renovation in Richmond?
A typical whole house renovation in Richmond involves a general contractor for project management and carpentry, flooring installer, painter, licensed electrician (required for panel or circuit work), licensed plumber (required for fixture changes), and tile setter for kitchen and bathroom work. Using a single renovation company that coordinates all trades under one contract simplifies scheduling and creates a single point of accountability for the entire project.

### Why should I choose Reno Stars for my Richmond renovation?
Reno Stars has completed multiple whole house renovations throughout Richmond, with direct experience in Richmond''s permit process, strata requirements, and local trade network. We offer fixed-contract pricing so your budget is confirmed at signing with no surprise change orders for standard scope items. We self-perform carpentry, painting, and project management, subcontracting only licensed trade work. Richmond clients rate our completed projects 4.9/5 based on post-completion surveys.


