### What specific renovation work was completed in this Richmond townhouse project?
This Richmond townhouse renovation encompassed two major renovation areas within a $75,000–$78,000 budget over 7–9 weeks. See our guide to [BC Strata Renovation Rules](/en/blog/strata-renovation-rules-vancouver/) for Metro Vancouver homeowners. The bathroom scope included two complete overhauls: one bathroom was converted from a bathtub to a modern shower, while the second underwent a full four-piece renovation with gray tiles, silver fixtures, and custom frameless glass doors. The kitchen scope delivered a modern kitchen renovation with updated cabinetry and surfaces. The project also included re-tiling the first floor, a whole-home repaint, and light fixture replacement throughout — ensuring every surface visible daily was updated in a single coordinated project.


