UPDATE blog_posts SET content_en = '<h2>Introduction</h2><p>In the scenic locale of [West Vancouver](/en/areas/west-vancouver/), a unique renovation project took place, transforming a single bathroom into two stylish and functional spaces. This case study explores the journey of this transformation, highlighting the challenges faced and the innovative solutions implemented by Reno Stars.</p><h2>Project Overview</h2><p>The scope of this project involved the transformation of one existing bathroom into two separate, stylish spaces. Our team undertook tasks such as cabinet installation, countertop replacement, backsplash tiling, plumbing, and lighting. With a budget of $57,000 - $60,000 and a timeline of 9-11 weeks, the project aimed to enhance both the aesthetics and usability of the bathrooms.</p><h2>Challenges</h2><p>The primary challenge was to efficiently divide the existing space into two separate bathrooms while maintaining a cohesive design. This required meticulous planning and execution to ensure that both spaces were not only functional but also visually appealing.</p><h2>Our Solution</h2><p>To address the challenge, our team carefully planned the layout, ensuring optimal use of the available space. We utilized high-quality materials, including full wall tiles and custom wood grain cabinets, to create a seamless and stylish look. Fresh paint was applied to enhance the overall ambiance, and attention was given to every detail, from plumbing to lighting, to ensure both bathrooms met the highest standards of functionality and design.</p><h2>Before & After</h2><div><img src="https://pub-b88db8c50fd64a9a87f60a4486a4a488.r2.dev/uploads/admin/social-ready-before-1-mmo6361e.jpg" alt="Transformation of One Bathroom into Two Stylish Spaces - Before Renovation 1"/><p>Before the renovation, the bathroom was a single, outdated space.</p></div><div><img src="https://pub-b88db8c50fd64a9a87f60a4486a4a488.r2.dev/uploads/admin/social-ready-after-2-mmo6361i.jpg" alt="Transforming One Bathroom into Two Stylish Spaces - After Renovation 1"/><p>After the renovation, the space was transformed into two modern, stylish bathrooms.</p></div><div><img src="https://pub-b88db8c50fd64a9a87f60a4486a4a488.r2.dev/uploads/admin/social-ready-after-3-mmo6361i.jpg" alt="Transforming One Bathroom into Two Stylish Spaces - After Renovation 2"/><img src="https://pub-b88db8c50fd64a9a87f60a4486a4a488.r2.dev/uploads/admin/social-ready-after-4-mmo6361i.jpg" alt="Transforming One Bathroom into Two Stylish Spaces - After Renovation 3"/><p>Each bathroom features custom wood grain cabinets and full wall tiles.</p></div><h2>Results & Key Takeaways</h2><p>The final outcome was a resounding success. The two new bathrooms are not only stylish but also highly functional, meeting the client''s needs and expectations. The cohesive design and quality craftsmanship have significantly enhanced the property''s value and appeal. This project demonstrates the importance of careful planning and the use of high-quality materials in achieving outstanding renovation results.</p>



For homeowners planning for the future or needing improved mobility, our [accessible bathroom renovations](/services/accessible-bathroom/) service includes grab bars, walk-in showers, wider doorways, and slip-resistant flooring.


Renovations that add high-draw appliances or modern lighting often benefit from a [critical load panel upgrade](/services/critical-load-panel/) to ensure adequate electrical capacity and safety.


If you live in a strata property (condo or townhouse), review BC''s [strata renovation rules](/blog/strata-renovation-rules-vancouver/) before starting work — many projects require strata council approval and must follow specific noise, hour, and contractor requirements.
## Frequently Asked Questions

### How do you convert a single bathroom into two separate stylish spaces in West Vancouver?
Converting one bathroom into two in a West Vancouver home requires splitting the existing plumbing zone and creating two independent functional spaces — each with its own wet area, ventilation, and distinct design identity. The key steps are: structural assessment of walls and floors for new partition placement, plumbing redesign to route independent supply and drain lines to each bathroom, separate exhaust ventilation for each space (required by BC Building Code), and independent design execution for each room. The result is two functional, aesthetically distinct bathrooms from one previously underutilized space.

### What challenges are unique to a West Vancouver bathroom split project?
West Vancouver homes often present specific challenges for bathroom conversions: mountainside properties have complex structural configurations; many West Vancouver homes have premium original construction that limits where walls can be cut or moved; water pressure and drain-to-stack distances are more variable in hillside properties; and the District of West Vancouver''s permit office has specific inspection protocols that contractors must follow. Experience with West Vancouver''s building stock is a meaningful differentiator when selecting a renovation contractor for this type of project.

### How much does it cost to create two bathrooms from one in West Vancouver?
Creating two stylish, functional bathrooms from one existing bathroom in West Vancouver typically costs $30,000–$60,000. Each resulting bathroom needs independent finishing (tile, vanity, fixtures, glass, accessories) — at $12,000–$22,000 per bathroom for quality finishes — plus the structural and plumbing conversion work ($6,000–$16,000). West Vancouver''s premium market expects premium execution, which pushes costs toward the higher end of this range. The investment is well-supported by West Vancouver property values and buyer expectations.

### What design approach creates two cohesive but distinct bathrooms from one space?
When creating two bathrooms from one, establishing a shared design language — consistent tile material, fixture finish (brushed nickel or matte black), and colour palette — while differentiating each room through layout and specific feature choices creates cohesion without monotony. Common approaches: one bathroom with a shower-only layout in a more spa-influenced style, the other with tub/shower combination in a more functional family configuration. Alternatively, one serves as a guest bathroom with statement tile, the other as a primary ensuite with a larger vanity and premium fixtures.

### What permits are required to split a bathroom in West Vancouver?
Splitting a bathroom in West Vancouver requires a District of West Vancouver building permit for the structural partition work, new plumbing rough-in (connecting to the existing stack system), new electrical circuits for lighting and exhaust fans in each bathroom, and ventilation to exterior. Consider our [Heat Pump Installation Vancouver](/en/services/heat-pump-hvac/) service to upgrade heating and cooling with modern energy-efficient systems. The permit application must include a plumbing diagram showing the new rough-in configuration and a floor plan showing the proposed layout of each resulting bathroom. District of West Vancouver permit processing for residential projects: typically 3–6 weeks.


