est Vancouver - After Renovation 2"></div><div><img src="https://pub-b88db8c50fd64a9a87f60a4486a4a488.r2.dev/uploads/admin/social-ready-before-3-mmpdnxiu.jpeg" alt="Stylish Kitchen Renovation with White Cabinets and Gold Handles - Before Renovation 3"><img src="https://pub-b88db8c50fd64a9a87f60a4486a4a488.r2.dev/uploads/admin/social-ready-after-3-mmpdnxiu.jpg" alt="Stylish Kitchen Renovation in West Vancouver - After Renovation 3"></div><h2>Results & Key Takeaways</h2><p>The final outcome was a stunning kitchen that exceeded the client''s expectations. The combination of white cabinets and gold handles, along with improved lighting and a fresh paint job, resulted in a modern and inviting space. The client was extremely satisfied with the timely completion and the quality of the work, making it an ideal setting for Airbnb guests.</p>



Many Metro Vancouver homeowners also upgrade to a [heat pump HVAC system](/services/heat-pump-hvac/) during renovations — providing efficient year-round heating and cooling while qualifying for CleanBC rebates.


Renovations that add high-draw appliances or modern lighting often benefit from a [critical load panel upgrade](/services/critical-load-panel/) to ensure adequate electrical capacity and safety.


For homeowners planning long-term or accommodating family members with mobility needs, [accessible bathroom renovations](/services/accessible-bathroom/) — including grab bars, curbless showers, and slip-resistant flooring — are a smart addition to any major renovation project.


If you live in a strata property (condo or townhouse), review BC''s [strata renovation rules](/blog/strata-renovation-rules-vancouver/) before starting work — many projects require strata council approval and must follow specific noise, hour, and contractor requirements.
## Frequently Asked Questions

### Why are white cabinets with gold handles a strong choice for a West Vancouver Airbnb kitchen?
White cabinets with gold hardware create a bright, welcoming aesthetic that photographs exceptionally well — critical for Airbnb listing photos where the kitchen is a primary filter for guests. The combination reads as premium without being aggressively trendy, appealing to a broad demographic of guests. In West Vancouver''s Airbnb rental market, where guests expect a high-quality environment proportionate to nightly rates, a well-designed kitchen with quality finishes directly supports occupancy rates and review scores.

### How much does a kitchen renovation for an Airbnb property cost in West Vancouver?
A kitchen renovation optimized for short-term rental in West Vancouver typically costs $22,000–$45,000, similar to a standard residential kitchen renovation at this price point. The specific priorities for an Airbnb kitchen are different: durability over cost (surfaces that withstand frequent use by different guests), simplicity of operation (intuitive appliances and layout), ease of cleaning (minimal grout lines, smooth countertop surfaces), and impressive first impressions (quality fixtures, good lighting). These priorities align well with a quality renovation approach.

### What kitchen features are most important for Airbnb guests in West Vancouver?
For West Vancouver Airbnb properties, the kitchen features that most impact guest satisfaction are: a high-quality range or cooktop (guests who book West Vancouver properties often cook elaborate meals), a large refrigerator with ample storage, a dishwasher (essential for multi-guest rentals), good counter workspace for meal preparation, adequate cookware and utensil storage, and natural or good artificial lighting. The aesthetic — white cabinets, gold hardware, quality countertops — sets the first impression and influences reviews even when guests do not cook extensively.

### Do gold hardware and fixtures require special maintenance in a rental property?
Brushed gold or satin gold hardware is a practical choice for short-term rental kitchens because the finish is more forgiving of fingerprints and surface wear than polished gold (which shows scratches more readily). Brushed gold cabinet pulls and handles should be wiped with a damp microfibre cloth between guest stays — no harsh chemicals required. Faucets in a brushed gold finish hold up well to regular cleaning with standard non-abrasive kitchen cleaners. Avoid bleach-based cleaners, which can discolour metal finishes over time.

### How long does a kitchen renovation take in West Vancouver?
A complete kitchen renovation in West Vancouver — custom or semi-custom cabinets, new countertops, backsplash, and fixtures — typically takes 10–16 weeks from contract signing. District of West Vancouver permit processing for kitchen plumbing and electrical changes: 3–5 weeks. Custom cabinet lead time: 6–10 weeks (overlap with permitting). Active construction after permit and cabinet delivery: 3–5 weeks. West Vancouver''s premium construction quality means renovation companies must meet higher workmanship standards than typical Metro Vancouver markets.

### What was the scope and budget of this West Vancouver Airbnb kitchen renovation?
This West Vancouver Airbnb kitchen renovation had a total budget of $29,000–$33,000 and was completed in 3–4 weeks of active construction — faster than the typical 10–16 week project timeline because material selections were finalized before construction began, allowing continuous work flow. The full scope of work included: cabinet installation (new white cabinets with gold hardware), countertop replacement, backsplash tiling, plumbing updates, and lighting enhancements. Older Metro Vancouver homes may also need our [Poly-B Pipe Replacement](/en/services/poly-b-replacement/) service to eliminate unsafe plastic piping. The tight timeline was a priority for the Airbnb owner, who needed to minimize the booking interruption window during renovation.


