ploads/admin/social-ready-before-2-mmmmctzc.png" alt="Kitchen Renovation - Before Renovation 2"><img src="https://pub-b88db8c50fd64a9a87f60a4486a4a488.r2.dev/uploads/admin/social-ready-after-2-mmmmctzc.jpg" alt="Modern bathroom featuring a marble shower, sleek vanity, and contemporary lighting."></div><div><img src="https://pub-b88db8c50fd64a9a87f60a4486a4a488.r2.dev/uploads/admin/social-ready-before-3-mmmmctzd.png" alt="Kitchen Renovation - Before Renovation 3"><img src="https://pub-b88db8c50fd64a9a87f60a4486a4a488.r2.dev/uploads/admin/social-ready-after-3-mmmmcul1.jpg" alt="Modern bathroom featuring a white tub and elegant marble walls with a showerhead."></div><h2>Results & Key Takeaways</h2><p>The final outcome was a pair of stunning bathrooms that perfectly blend functionality with style. The client was thrilled with the transformation, noting the improved usability and modern aesthetic. This project highlights the importance of thoughtful design and quality materials in achieving a successful renovation.</p>



Many Metro Vancouver homeowners also upgrade to a [heat pump HVAC system](/services/heat-pump-hvac/) during renovations — providing efficient year-round heating and cooling while qualifying for CleanBC rebates.


Renovations that add high-draw appliances or modern lighting often benefit from a [critical load panel upgrade](/services/critical-load-panel/) to ensure adequate electrical capacity and safety.
## Frequently Asked Questions

### How much does a two-[bathroom renovation cost](/en/guides/bathroom-renovation-cost-vancouver/) in a Burnaby townhouse?
A dual [bathroom renovation](/en/services/bathroom/) in a Burnaby townhouse (both bathrooms renovated simultaneously) typically costs $22,000–$48,000 at mid-range finishes. Renovating two bathrooms together achieves 10–20% cost savings compared to phasing them separately, through batched trade scheduling, combined material orders, and single contractor mobilization. Family-friendly design elements (durable tile, practical storage, accessible fixture heights) can be incorporated without premium cost impact.

### What family-friendly features should be included in a Burnaby bathroom renovation?
Family-friendly bathroom features for a Burnaby townhouse include: durable porcelain tile (not natural stone, which is more porous and harder to maintain with children), shower-tub combination in at least one bathroom (essential for bathing young children), ample storage (recessed niche in the shower, vanity drawer storage, medicine cabinet), grab bar-compatible walls (blocking behind tile for future grab bar installation), and slip-resistant tile finish for the shower and tub floor area (minimum R10 coefficient of friction for wet areas).

### How long does it take to renovate two bathrooms in a Burnaby townhouse?
Renovating two bathrooms simultaneously in a Burnaby townhouse typically takes 5–8 weeks of active construction: demo week one, plumbing and electrical rough-in (inspected) weeks two to three, tile installation weeks three to five, and vanity, glass, fixtures, and finishing weeks five to seven. Older Metro Vancouver homes may also need our [Poly-B Pipe Replacement](/en/services/poly-b-replacement/) service to eliminate unsafe plastic piping. Strata approval for Burnaby townhouses adds 3–5 weeks before construction begins. Total timeline from contract signing: 8–12 weeks.

### Does renovating both bathrooms at once disrupt family life more than phasing?
Renovating both bathrooms simultaneously requires more upfront planning for temporary bathroom access (typically using a main floor powder room or a temporary arrangement with neighbours or family). However, the disruption is compressed to one 5–8 week period rather than two separate disruption periods spread over months or years. Most Burnaby families find one concentrated renovation period less stressful than two separate projects, particularly with young children.

### What makes Reno Stars a strong choice for a Burnaby family bathroom renovation?
Reno Stars has completed numerous multi-bathroom renovation projects in Burnaby, with direct experience managing strata approval requirements and coordinating multiple trades efficiently. Our fixed-price contracts lock in the budget at signing. We use a dedicated project manager who maintains clear communication with homeowners throughout the process — particularly important for families with children living in the home during renovation. Burnaby bathroom renovation clients rate our work 4.9/5 for quality and communication.

### What tile and fixture finishes were used in this Burnaby bathroom renovation?
This Burnaby townhouse bathroom renovation featured white porcelain tiles paired with brushed gold fixtures — a combination that delivers a warm contemporary look while remaining practical for a family environment. See our guide to [BC Strata Renovation Rules](/en/blog/strata-renovation-rules-vancouver/) for Metro Vancouver homeowners. Frameless glass shower doors maximize the visual space in the main bathroom. White tile provides a neutral base that is easy to maintain and will not date quickly. Brushed gold hardware (as opposed to polished chrome) is more forgiving of water spots and fingerprints in a busy family bathroom. The tub-to-shower conversion was applied to one bathroom while preserving the bathtub in the second — an important consideration for families with young children who still require a bathing option.

