## Frequently Asked Questions

**How much does a bathroom renovation cost in Surrey in 2026?**
Budget bathroom refreshes in Surrey: $13,000–$22,000. Mid-range full renovations: $22,000–$38,000. High-end ensuite renovations: $38,000–$65,000. Powder rooms: $8,000–$16,000.

**How long does a bathroom renovation take in Surrey?**
Budget refreshes: 2–4 weeks. Mid-range: 4–7 weeks (including 2–4 weeks for City of Surrey permit). High-end ensuite: 6–10 weeks. Strata projects add 4–8 weeks for council approval.

**Do I need a City of Surrey permit to renovate my bathroom?**
Yes, if you''re moving plumbing, upgrading electrical, or modifying walls. The City of Surrey''s eBuild portal accepts online permit applications. Simple bathroom refreshes (tile, vanity replacement without moving plumbing) typically don''t require a permit.

**Does Reno Stars serve all Surrey neighbourhoods?**
Yes — we serve all of Surrey including Newton, Fleetwood, Cloverdale, Whalley/City Centre, South Surrey (Morgan Crossing, Grandview, Elgin), Clayton, and Panorama Ridge. Surrey is one of our highest-volume service areas.

**What''s the most popular bathroom renovation in Surrey right now?**
Converting an old tub/shower combo to a walk-in shower in the primary ensuite, plus upgrading the main bathroom to a new vanity and tile. Our [Accessible Bathroom Renovation](/en/services/accessible-bathroom/) service specialises in safety upgrades and accessibility modifications. This two-bathroom package costs $35,000–$55,000 total and is particularly popular in South Surrey''s larger homes and Fleetwood''s 1990s–2000s detached houses.

**What special considerations apply to Surrey strata townhome bathroom renovations?**
Surrey strata townhome bathroom renovations — especially Clayton and Willoughby townhomes — require strata council approval before starting work. The process: submit a renovation application with scope description, contractor credentials (BC Housing license, WCB clearance, $2M liability insurance), and floor plan. Approval takes 4–8 weeks for typical Surrey stratas. Critical point: Surrey townhomes frequently have shared plumbing walls between units. Consult your strata manager before any work on supply or drain lines — changes to shared plumbing require strata engineer sign-off. Older Metro Vancouver homes may also need our [Poly-B Pipe Replacement](/en/services/poly-b-replacement/) service to eliminate unsafe plastic piping. See our guide to [BC Strata Renovation Rules](/en/blog/strata-renovation-rules-vancouver/) for Metro Vancouver homeowners.



