Based on real projects completed by Reno Stars across Richmond — from Steveston townhouses to Sea Island condos — completed bathroom renovations have ranged from: minimalist wall-hung vanity, frameless shower, subway tile: $15,000–$18,000 (2–3 weeks); gray tile full gut with rainfall shower and porcelain throughout: $17,000–$20,000 (4–5 weeks). See our guide to [BC Strata Renovation Rules](/fa/blog/strata-renovation-rules-vancouver/) for Metro Vancouver homeowners. These real project data points reflect what Richmond homeowners are actually spending at the most popular renovation tiers — not theoretical ranges. The total cost is driven primarily by tile selection (large-format porcelain costs more than subway tile), shower complexity (rainfall head and niche vs standard showerhead), and vanity style (wall-hung vs freestanding vs built-in). Requesting a detailed line-item quote ensures the estimate reflects your specific Richmond bathroom''s actual scope.


