## Frequently Asked Questions

**How much does a kitchen renovation cost in West Vancouver in 2026?**
Entry-level West Vancouver kitchen renovations start around $30,000–$50,000. Mid-range projects run $50,000–$100,000. High-end custom kitchens in British Properties or Cypress Park typically run $100,000–$250,000+.

**Do I need a heritage review for my West Van kitchen renovation?**
Only if your property is on the District of West Vancouver Heritage Register AND your renovation involves exterior changes or structural alterations visible from the exterior. Standard interior kitchen renovations (cabinetry, countertops, appliances) in heritage homes are generally unrestricted. Consult the District''s Heritage Advisory Committee if you''re removing walls.

**How long does a high-end kitchen renovation take in West Vancouver?**
Allow 2–5 weeks for permits, 8–16 weeks for custom cabinetry fabrication (often from local BC cabinet makers or European imports), and 6–12 weeks of construction. Total timeline for high-end projects: 4–9 months from design sign-off to completion.

**Does Reno Stars do kitchen renovations in the British Properties?**
Yes — we have experience with luxury kitchen renovations throughout West Vancouver, including British Properties, Cypress Park, and Ambleside heritage homes. Our project managers are experienced with the District of West Vancouver''s permit process and heritage considerations.

**What''s different about renovating a kitchen in West Vancouver vs. Vancouver?**
Material expectations are higher — quartz is baseline, natural stone is common. Appliances are typically professional-grade (Sub-Zero, Wolf, Miele). Structural view work is much more common. And the District of West Vancouver''s permit office has specific requirements for heritage properties that don''t exist in Vancouver proper.

