UPDATE blog_posts SET content_en = '**Kitchen renovations in North Vancouver** cost $17,000–$95,000 in 2026 depending on scope. A budget refresh (existing layout, semi-custom cabinets, new countertops and backsplash) starts at $17,000–$29,000. A mid-range full replacement for a typical District rancher or City condo runs $29,000–$50,000. High-end projects in upper Lynn Valley, Edgemont, or mountain-view homes start at $50,000 and scale higher for custom millwork and premium appliances. North Vancouver commands a 5–10% labour premium over South-of-Fraser cities due to local trade wages and logistics.

North Vancouver — comprising both the City of North Vancouver and the District of North Vancouver — sits across Burrard Inlet from downtown Vancouver, offering residents spectacular mountain and city views, proximity to world-class outdoor recreation, and a distinctly West Coast character. For kitchen renovations, North Vancouver presents a fascinating mix: heritage homes in Lower Lonsdale, mid-century ranchers on the District''s flat areas, luxury mountain-view properties in the upper reaches, and a significant strata condo inventory along the Lonsdale corridor.

## North Vancouver Housing Stock

- **Heritage and early post-war homes (City of North Van, Lower Lonsdale)**: Older homes built 1920–1960 near Lonsdale Avenue. Many have galvanized or original copper plumbing, 60–100A electrical panels, and character kitchens that benefit from updating. Our [Critical Load Panel Installation](/en/services/critical-load-panel/) service upgrades your home electrical capacity for modern renovation demands.
- **Mid-century ranchers (Lynn Valley, Capilano)**: 1950s–1970s District homes on larger lots. Generally well-configured with solid structural bones; often the kitchens are small relative to the home''s overall size — prime candidates for expansion.
- **Newer stratas (Lonsdale Quay, Central Lonsdale)**: Post-1990 concrete and wood-frame condos along the Seabus-adjacent Lonsdale corridor. Modern services, strata-governed renovations.
- **Mountain-view luxury homes (upper Lynn Valley, Edgemont, Mosquito Creek)**: High-end properties with dramatic views and premium renovation budgets.
- **Strata townhomes (Seymour, Windsor Park)**: 1990s–2010s townhome strata with more renovation flexibility than high-rise condos.

## Kitchen Renovation Costs in North Vancouver (2026)

### Budget Kitchen Renovation: $17,000–$29,000

Refresh without major layout changes:

- Cabinet refacing or semi-custom replacement: $5,000–$8,500
- Quartz or laminate countertops: $3,500–$6,500
- Tile backsplash: $1,500–$2,800
- Sink and faucet: $600–$1,200
- Standard appliance package: $3,500–$6,500
- New lighting: $1,000–$2,000

**North Van premium note**: North Vancouver generally commands a 5–10% labour premium over Surrey or Langley due to higher local wages and longer travel times for some contractors. This is factored into the ranges above.

### Mid-Range Kitchen Renovation: $29,000–$50,000

Full replacement for North Vancouver''s 1970s–1990s family homes and ranchers:

- Semi-custom cabinetry: $13,000–$21,000
- Quartz countertops + island: $6,000–$11,000
- Kitchen island: $3,500–$7,000
- Appliance package (mid-tier): $6,000–$12,000
- Plumbing: $1,500–$3,500
- Electrical: $1,500–$3,000
- City/District of North Vancouver permit: $400–$900

**Note on jurisdiction**: The City of North Vancouver (City of Lonsdale) and the District of North Vancouver (Lynn Valley, Deep Cove, Capilano) are separate municipalities with separate building departments. Your permit is issued by the municipality whose boundaries your property falls within.

### High-End Kitchen Renovation: $50,000–$95,000

Mountain-view homes in upper Lynn Valley, Edgemont Village, and the Grouse Mountain slopes often merit premium kitchen investments:

- Custom cabinetry with view-framing design: $25,000–$45,000
- Natural stone countertops: $9,000–$18,000
- Professional appliances (Wolf, Miele, Sub-Zero): $12,000–$25,000
- View-maximizing window addition: $8,000–$20,000
