## Frequently Asked Questions

**How much does a kitchen renovation cost in North Vancouver in 2026?**
Budget kitchen renovations in North Vancouver: $17,000–$29,000. Mid-range full replacements: $29,000–$50,000. High-end mountain-view kitchens: $50,000–$95,000. North Van labour runs 5–10% above Metro Vancouver average.

**Is my property in the City or District of North Vancouver?**
Check your property tax notice or BC Assessment record — both list the municipality. Generally: Lower and Central Lonsdale = City of North Van; Lynn Valley, Deep Cove, Capilano, Seymour = District of North Van.

**Do I need to check for Poly-B plumbing before renovating?**
Yes — if your North Vancouver strata was built before 2000, it likely has Poly-B supply lines, which are prone to failure. We assess Poly-B condition as part of every pre-renovation consultation in affected buildings.

**How long does a North Vancouver kitchen renovation take?**
Budget: 3–6 weeks. Mid-range: 6–10 weeks (plus 2–5 weeks for permit). High-end view kitchens: 10–18 weeks. Strata projects add 4–8 weeks for council approval.

**Can Reno Stars handle the strata application for my North Van condo renovation?**
Yes — we prepare complete strata application packages including drawings, material specs, WCB clearance, and liability insurance certificates. We''ve worked with strata corporations throughout the Lonsdale corridor. See our guide to [BC Strata Renovation Rules](/en/blog/strata-renovation-rules-vancouver/) for Metro Vancouver homeowners.

**What permits are required for a North Vancouver kitchen renovation?**
Permits are required in North Vancouver when a kitchen renovation involves: (1) Moving the kitchen sink or dishwasher (plumbing permit from either the City of North Vancouver or the District of North Vancouver, depending on your address). (2) Adding or modifying electrical circuits — new dedicated appliance circuits, island outlets, under-cabinet lighting on new circuits. (3) Removing load-bearing walls (structural permit, engineering drawing required). Cabinet replacement, countertop swaps, new backsplash tile, and appliance replacement with no plumbing or electrical changes do not require a permit.



