North Vancouver — comprising both the City of North Vancouver and the District of North Vancouver — sits across Burrard Inlet from downtown Vancouver, offering residents spectacular mountain and city views, proximity to world-class outdoor recreation, and a distinctly West Coast character. For kitchen renovations, North Vancouver presents a fascinating mix: heritage homes in Lower Lonsdale, mid-century ranchers on the District''s flat areas, luxury mountain-view properties in the upper reaches, and a significant strata condo inventory along the Lonsdale corridor.

## North Vancouver Housing Stock

- **Heritage and early post-war homes (City of North Van, Lower Lonsdale)**: Older homes built 1920–1960 near Lonsdale Avenue. Many have galvanized or original copper plumbing, 60–100A electrical panels, and character kitchens that benefit from updating. Our [Critical Load Panel Installation](/en/services/critical-load-panel/) service upgrades your home electrical capacity for modern renovation demands.
- **Mid-century ranchers (Lynn Valley, Capilano)**: 1950s–1970s District homes on larger lots. Generally well-configured with solid structural bones; often the kitchens are small relative to the home''s overall size — prime candidates for expansion.
- **Newer stratas (Lonsdale Quay, Central Lonsdale)**: Post-1990 concrete and wood-frame condos along the Seabus-adjacent Lonsdale corridor. Modern services, strata-governed renovations.
- **Mountain-view luxury homes (upper Lynn Valley, Edgemont, Mosquito Creek)**: High-end properties with dramatic views and premium renovation budgets.
- **Strata townhomes (Seymour, Windsor Park)**: 1990s–2010s townhome strata with more renovation flexibility than high-rise condos.

