## Port Moody Housing Stock

- **Heritage and early character homes (near Rocky Point, St. Johns Street)**: 1940s–1970s homes within walking distance of the waterfront. These often have 60–100A panels and older plumbing that benefits from upgrading during renovation.
- **1980s–1990s detached homes (Heritage Mountain, College Park)**: Well-built suburban homes with modern electrical and plumbing — the most renovation-ready segment of Port Moody''s housing stock.
- **Post-2000 townhomes (Klahanie, Pleasantside)**: Newer strata townhomes with modern services; renovation requires strata council approval.
- **Inlet Centre condos (2005–present)**: High-rise and mid-rise concrete condos adjacent to the Evergreen Line. Strata-governed, modern building systems.
- **Barnet Marine Park area**: Some older waterfront and near-waterfront properties with views of the inlet.

## Kitchen Renovation Costs in Port Moody (2026)

### Budget Kitchen Renovation: $16,000–$27,000

