UPDATE blog_posts SET content_en = 'Maple Ridge is Metro Vancouver''s easternmost city — a rapidly growing community along the Fraser River that still retains a semi-rural character. With large lots, newer suburban subdivisions, and some of the most affordable detached housing in the region, Maple Ridge offers renovation opportunities at price points that are more accessible than the inner-ring suburbs. Our [Accessible Bathroom Renovation](/en/services/accessible-bathroom/) service specialises in safety upgrades and accessibility modifications. This guide covers kitchen and bathroom renovation costs in Maple Ridge for 2026.

## Maple Ridge Housing Stock

- **Central Maple Ridge (older core)**: 1960s–1990s single-family homes near the historic downtown on 224th Street. Mix of older character homes and tract-built suburban houses. Older electrical panels (60–100A) common in pre-1980 homes.
- **Hammond and Ruskin**: Lower-lying areas near the river, older housing stock with renovation potential.
- **Silver Valley and Albion**: Newer subdivisions (2000s–2015) on the hillside. Well-serviced homes with modern electrical (200A) and plumbing — easiest homes to renovate.
- **Cottonwood and Thornhill**: Larger lots, mix of acreage and suburban homes. Some properties on septic systems (important for kitchen waste considerations).
- **Townhomes (Town Centre, Port Haney)**: Newer strata developments in the walkable downtown area. See our guide to [BC Strata Renovation Rules](/en/blog/strata-renovation-rules-vancouver/) for Metro Vancouver homeowners.

## Kitchen Renovation Costs in Maple Ridge (2026)

### Budget Kitchen Renovation: $15,000–$26,000

Maple Ridge''s more affordable housing market means budget renovations deliver high relative value:

- Semi-custom cabinetry or refacing: $4,000–$7,500
- Laminate or entry quartz countertops: $2,800–$5,500
- Tile backsplash: $1,200–$2,200
- Sink and faucet: $550–$1,000
- Standard appliance package: $3,000–$5,500
- Lighting upgrades: $800–$1,600

**Older home note**: Pre-1980 Maple Ridge homes frequently have 60A or 100A electrical panels — insufficient for modern kitchens with induction cooktops, dishwashers, and refrigerators all running simultaneously. Budget $1,500–$4,000 for a panel upgrade to 200A.

### Mid-Range Kitchen Renovation: $26,000–$43,000

Full kitchen replacement for Maple Ridge''s family homes:

- Semi-custom cabinetry: $10,000–$17,000
- Quartz countertops + island: $5,000–$9,000
- Kitchen island: $2,800–$6,000
- Appliance package (mid-tier): $5,000–$10,500
- Plumbing: $1,100–$2,800
- Electrical: $1,100–$2,600
- City of Maple Ridge building permit: $330–$720

### High-End Kitchen Renovation: $43,000–$72,000

For Maple Ridge''s larger Silver Valley and Albion homes or acreage properties:

- Custom cabinetry: $18,000–$32,000
- Stone countertops: $6,500–$13,000
- Professional appliances: $9,000–$18,000
- Heated floors: $2,000–$4,000
- Layout reconfiguration: $4,000–$8,000

## Bathroom Renovation Costs in Maple Ridge (2026)

### Budget Bathroom: $12,000–$20,000
- Tub/shower re-tile: $2,800–$5,500
- New vanity and fixtures: $1,800–$3,800
- Toilet: $450–$900
- Flooring tile: $1,100–$2,200

### Mid-Range Bathroom: $20,000–$34,000
- Full gut and rebuild:
- New tile throughout: $4,000–$7,500
- Custom vanity: $2,500–$5,500
- Walk-in shower: $4,500–$9,000
- Heated floors: $1,600–$3,200
- Permit (if moving plumbing): $230–$550

### High-End Primary Bathroom: $34,000–$58,000
- Soaker tub: $2,800–$6,500
- Frameless glass: $3,000–$6,500
- Custom double vanity: $4,500–$10,000
- Steam shower: $3,000–$6,500

## City of Maple Ridge Permit Requirements (2026)

**Permit required for:**
- Plumbing additions or relocations
- Electrical panel upgrades or new circuits
- Structural wall modifications
- Gas line additions

**No permit required for:**
- Cabinet replacement (same location)
- Countertop and backsplash replacement
- Appliance swap
- Painting and tile (non-structural)

**2026 permit fees (City of Maple Ridge):**
- Minor kitchen: $280–$580
- Kitchen with plumbing: $380–$800
- Bathroom with plumbing: $260–$600
- 200A electrical upgrade: $150–$320

**Processing time**: 2–3 weeks typically. Maple Ridge has a user-friendly online portal for residential permit applications.

**Septic system note**: Homes on septic systems in Maple Ridge''s rural areas need a septic assessment before any significant kitchen (or bathroom) expansion — adding fixtures or changing kitchen waste loads can require septic system upgrades. Contact Maple Ridge Development Services for guidance.

