## Frequently Asked Questions

### What is the best pre-sale renovation for a Port Moody home in 2026?
Basement suite legalization delivers the highest ROI in Port Moody at 180–225%: cost $22,000–$42,000, value added $48,000–$95,000. Kitchen renovation is the next best at 160–175% ROI ($32,000–$58,000 cost, $52,000–$95,000 value added). For Heritage Mountain and Moody Centre homes built 1978–1995, Poly-B pipe replacement ($8,000–$18,000) is often the most important foundational investment before listing.

### How much does a pre-sale kitchen renovation cost in Port Moody?
A full kitchen renovation in Port Moody runs $32,000–$58,000 and typically adds $52,000–$95,000 in value — a 160–175% return. Port Moody''s Heritage Mountain market expects premium finishes: custom cabinetry, quartz countertops, and professional ventilation. Allow 4–6 weeks for a complete kitchen renovation plus permit processing.

### Does Poly-B plumbing affect home sale value in Port Moody?
Significantly. Port Moody has high Poly-B prevalence in homes built 1978–1995, and insurers increasingly decline coverage for homes with Poly-B. Buyers and their lenders flag it during inspection, often resulting in $20,000–$40,000 price reductions or subject-to-removal conditions. Full replacement costs $8,000–$18,000 for a detached home — nearly always worthwhile before listing.

### When should I start a pre-sale renovation to list in Port Moody''s spring market?
Begin in January for a March–May spring listing. A complete kitchen + bathroom renovation takes 6–9 weeks including permit processing. Add 2–3 weeks if Poly-B replacement or an electrical panel upgrade (100A → 200A at $3,500–$5,500) is needed. Older Metro Vancouver homes may also need our [Poly-B Pipe Replacement](/en/services/poly-b-replacement/) service to eliminate unsafe plastic piping. Port Moody''s tech-sector buyer demographic also responds well to EV-charging-ready panels, which can be included in the electrical upgrade. Our [Critical Load Panel Installation](/en/services/critical-load-panel/) service upgrades your home electrical capacity for modern renovation demands.
### What is the ROI on a master ensuite renovation for pre-sale in Port Moody?

A master ensuite renovation for pre-sale in Port Moody costs $22,000–$42,000 and adds $35,000–$68,000 in sale value — a return of 155–165%. Port Moody''s tech-sector and professional buyer demographic has high finish expectations; a dated ensuite is the single most common buyer objection in this market. A walk-in shower conversion with frameless glass, heated floors, and custom vanity is the typical scope that achieves the upper end of this value range. Our [Accessible Bathroom Renovation](/en/services/accessible-bathroom/) service specialises in safety upgrades and accessibility modifications.

### What is the ROI on a deck renovation for pre-sale in Port Moody?

Port Moody is unique among Metro Vancouver cities: deck and outdoor space renovations deliver higher pre-sale ROI here than in most other markets, due to inlet and mountain views. A deck renovation costs $12,000–$35,000 and adds $20,000–$55,000 in value — 155–165% return. The inlet-view premium is real: a well-renovated outdoor entertaining space on an inlet-facing lot adds substantially more value than the same renovation on an inland property. Composite decking (Trex or similar) is the recommended material — it holds up to West Coast moisture far better than pressure-treated wood.



