UPDATE blog_posts SET content_en = 'Cabinet resurfacing in [Langley](/en/areas/langley/) costs **$4,000–$15,000** for painting or refacing, and **$18,000–$45,000+** if you replace cabinets outright. The right option depends on cabinet material, the door style you want, and whether you''re also updating countertops. Below are real 2026 prices from our Fraser Valley projects plus clear guidance for Walnut Grove, Willoughby, Fort Langley, Brookswood, and Aldergrove kitchens.

## What Cabinet Resurfacing Includes

Cabinet resurfacing (also called refinishing or refacing) keeps existing cabinet boxes and updates the visible parts: doors, drawer fronts, end panels, hardware, and sometimes face frames. The boxes and kitchen layout stay. What changes is everything you see when you walk in.

In Langley, this is the right move for the bulk of homes built between 1995 and 2015 — the underlying plywood or MDF boxes are structurally fine, but doors, hinges, and hardware look dated after 15–30 years.

## Cabinet Resurfacing Costs in Langley (2026)

| Option | Cost Range | Timeline | What''s Included |
|-' || '-' || '-|-' || '-' || '-|-' || '-' || '-|-' || '-' || '-|
| **Cabinet Painting** | $4,000–$8,000 | 5–7 days | Spray-finished doors + boxes, bonding primer, two finish coats. Hardware reuse or basic upgrade. |
| **Door Refacing** | $8,000–$15,000 | 1–2 weeks | Factory-finished shaker or slab doors + drawer fronts on existing boxes, matching end panels, soft-close hinges, new handles. |
| **Full Replacement** | $18,000–$45,000+ | 3–6 weeks | All cabinets removed and replaced. New boxes, doors, soft-close hinges, interior organizers. |

Add **$3,000–$8,000** if you''re also replacing the countertop. The counter has to come off for refacing — bundle or pay for disruption twice.

Real Langley and Fraser Valley kitchen project costs:

- **Langley white shaker kitchen** — $20,000–$23,000 over 4–5 weeks (full replacement, stock shaker doors, quartz counter). See [this Langley project](/en/projects/modern-kitchen-renovation-langley/).
- **Langley waterfall-island kitchen** — $28,000–$30,000 over 4–6 weeks (full replacement, semi-custom cabinets, waterfall quartz island). See the [waterfall island project](/en/projects/langley-kitchen-renovation-waterfall-island-design/).
- **Langley modern quartz kitchen** — $32,000–$35,000 over 3–4 weeks (semi-custom, quartz counter, modern slab doors).
- **Surrey custom shaker kitchen** — $29,000–$31,000 over 4–5 weeks (semi-custom, full soft-close).
- **Coquitlam budget-friendly kitchen** — $25,000–$27,000 over 5–6 weeks (full replacement).

Browse more [kitchen renovation projects](/en/services/kitchen/) for photos.

## Painting vs Refacing vs Replacing — Langley Decision Guide

**Choose painting if:**
- Boxes and doors are solid wood or MDF (we test on-site — thermofoil and melamine don''t hold paint)
- You like the existing door style but not the colour
- Budget is under $8,000
- Timeline is tight (under 2 weeks)

**Choose refacing if:**
- Boxes are good but doors are chipped, warped, delaminated, or very dated
- You want a different door style (raised-panel → shaker, cathedral-arch → slab)
- You want soft-close hinges and fresh hardware included
- Budget is $8,000–$15,000

**Choose full replacement if:**
- Boxes are swelling, water-damaged, or particle board is degrading
- You want to change layout (add an island, remove a peninsula, open to the dining room) — common in late-1990s Walnut Grove
- You''re doing a full kitchen reno with new counters, backsplash, electrical, and plumbing

## Langley Kitchens by Neighborhood

**Walnut Grove (1995–2005)** — typical kitchen has oak or maple raised-panel doors with plywood boxes and laminate counters. Both paint and reface beautifully. Painting to white or light grey is the single biggest visual change. Many Walnut Grove kitchens are large (30–45 linear feet), so budgets skew toward the top of the painting range.

**Willoughby and Yorkson (2005–present)** — cherry, espresso, or maple shaker doors with plywood boxes. Doors age well; most requests are painting to a lighter neutral. Dark-stain-to-light-paint needs a stain-blocking primer (add $300–$500).

**Fort Langley (mix of original heritage and 2000s reno)** — varies widely. Heritage homes often have real wood face-framed cabinets that take paint beautifully. 2000s renos may have thermofoil that won''t hold paint — test first.

**Brookswood and Murrayville (1980s–early 2000s)** — often oak or maple with cathedral-arch doors and tile counters. Refacing + quartz counter is usually the right combo. For pre-1985 originals, full replacement is often more cost-effective once you factor in degraded particle-board bases.

**Aldergrove (mix)** — many 1970s originals and 1990s renos. Test carefully before painting; lots of early-2000s thermofoil updates.

**Strata townhomes** in Willoughby: refacing or painting is almost always easier to get strata approval than full replacement since no plumbing or electrical work is involved. Our [Critical Load Panel Installation](/en/services/critical-load-panel/) service upgrades your home electrical capacity for modern renovation demands. See our guide to [BC Strata Renovation Rules](/en/blog/strata-renovation-rules-vancouver/) for Metro Vancouver homeowners.

## Our Langley Cabinet Resurfacing Process

1. **Free in-home consultation** — measure every cabinet, test door material, check box condition, discuss colour, door style, and hardware. Fixed written quote within 2–3 business days.
2. **Material selection** — visit our [Richmond showroom](/en/areas/richmond/) for door samples, colour chips, and hardware. Confirm profile, finish, hinges, and handles in writing.
3. **Site prep** — floors, appliances, and open-plan living areas covered with heavy plastic and rosin paper. Temporary dust barriers for open-concept kitchens.
4. **Dismantle** — doors, drawer fronts, hinges, and hardware removed and labeled for reinstall.
5. **Painting**: clean, sand, bonding primer, two finish coats sprayed in our shop. Reinstalled 5–7 days later. **Refacing**: factory-finished doors and drawer fronts arrive, end panels cut on-site, soft-close hinges and handles installed.
6. **Walk-through** — on-the-spot touch-ups and written warranty.

## ROI in Langley

Langley home prices span a wide range — **$850K townhomes** in Willoughby, **$1.3M detached homes** in Walnut Grove, **$1.6M+ acreages** in Fort Langley and Brookswood. A **$6,000 painted kitchen** returns 60–80% of cost at sale and makes MLS photos pop. A **$12,000 refaced kitchen** is often the difference between a stale listing and a quick sale, especially for 1990s Walnut Grove homes with oak cathedral-arch doors.

Staying 5+ years: full replacement gives you soft-close drawers, full-height pantry organization, and a modern layout for a decade. Under 2 years: painting or refacing is the right call. See our [pre-sale renovation guide](/en/blog/pre-sale-renovation-vancouver-what-to-fix-before-listing/) and [renovate-vs-move guide](/en/blog/renovate-vs-move-vancouver-2026/).



Metro Vancouver homeowners increasingly include a [heat pump HVAC upgrade](/services/heat-pump-hvac/) in their renovation plans — these systems provide efficient heating and cooling year-round, and qualify for BC Hydro and CleanBC rebate programs.


For homeowners planning long-term or accommodating family members with mobility needs, [accessible bathroom renovations](/services/accessible-bathroom/) — including grab bars, curbless showers, and slip-resistant flooring — are a smart addition to any major renovation project.
## Frequently Asked Questions

### Can oak cabinets be painted white in Langley?
Yes, but oak has prominent grain that shows through a single paint coat. For a smooth white finish, we add grain filler and an extra primer coat (+$500–$800 on a standard painting quote). Or skip the extra step for a subtle wood-grain look under the white — still very popular in 2026 for farmhouse kitchens.

### Does cabinet refacing make sense in Willoughby shaker kitchens?
Usually no — Willoughby shaker doors are already the style most homeowners want; refacing doesn''t add visual impact. Painting to a lighter colour is the high-ROI move. Refacing makes sense only if the doors themselves are damaged or if you want soft-close hinges and new hardware.

### How long does painting vs refacing take in Langley?
Painting: 5–7 days on-site (we spray the doors in our shop). Refacing: 1–2 weeks on-site (doors take 2–3 weeks to order, then 2–3 days install). Full replacement: 3–6 weeks on-site. You''ll "camp" with fridge + microwave + essentials tote during the work.

### Do you do permits in Langley?
No permit needed for painting or refacing. Full replacement that moves plumbing (sink relocation) or electrical (new range circuit) needs plumbing and/or electrical permits from the Township of Langley or City of Langley — we pull them for you. Older Metro Vancouver homes may also need our [Poly-B Pipe Replacement](/en/services/poly-b-replacement/) service to eliminate unsafe plastic piping. See our [BC renovation permits guide](/en/blog/renovation-permits-bc-guide/) | [Vancouver Renovation Cost Guide 2026](/en/blog/renovation-cost-vancouver-2026-complete-guide/) | [How to Choose a Contractor](/en/blog/how-to-choose-renovation-contractor-vancouver/) | [Pre-Sale Renovation Advice](/en/services/realtor/) | [Renovation Timeline Guide](/en/blog/renovation-timeline-how-long-does-each-project-take/).

### Do you serve Surrey and Abbotsford too?
Yes — we cover Surrey, White Rock, and Abbotsford at Langley pricing. No travel surcharge within the Fraser Valley.

### Do you have a dedicated guide for other cities?
Yes. See our guides for [Vancouver cabinet refinishing](/en/blog/cabinet-refinishing-vancouver-cost-guide/), [Burnaby cabinet refinishing](/en/blog/cabinet-refinishing-burnaby-cost-guide/), [Richmond cabinet refinishing](/en/blog/cabinet-refinishing-richmond-cost-guide/), [Surrey cabinet refinishing](/en/blog/cabinet-refinishing-surrey-cost-guide/), [Coquitlam cabinet refinishing](/en/blog/cabinet-refinishing-coquitlam-cost-guide/), [Port Coquitlam cabinet refinishing](/en/blog/cabinet-refinishing-port-coquitlam-cost-guide/), [Delta cabinet refinishing](/en/blog/cabinet-refinishing-delta-cost-guide/), [New Westminster cabinet refinishing](/en/blog/cabinet-refinishing-new-westminster-cost-guide/), [North Vancouver cabinet refinishing](/en/blog/cabinet-refinishing-north-vancouver-cost-guide/), [West Vancouver cabinet refinishing](/en/blog/cabinet-refinishing-west-vancouver-cost-guide/), [White Rock cabinet refinishing](/en/blog/cabinet-refinishing-white-rock-cost-guide/), [Maple Ridge cabinet refinishing](/en/blog/cabinet-refinishing-maple-ridge-cost-guide/), and [Port Moody cabinet resurfacing](/en/blog/cabinet-resurfacing-port-moody-cost-guide/).

