UPDATE blog_posts SET content_en = 'Langley — encompassing both the Township of Langley and the City of Langley — is one of Metro Vancouver''s fastest-growing communities. A blend of historic farmland, new master-planned subdivisions (Willoughby, Murrayville, Brookswood), and the vibrant Langley City core makes it a diverse renovation market. With competitive housing prices and a strong culture of homeownership, Langley has become one of Reno Stars'' busiest service areas for bathroom and kitchen renovations. [Cabinet refinishing](/en/services/cabinet/) is a cost-effective option for updating kitchen cabinets.

## Langley''s Housing Landscape

The Township and City of Langley have distinctly different housing profiles:

**Township of Langley (most of the area):**
- **Willoughby Heights (2000s–2020s)**: Metro Vancouver''s largest master-planned new development. Primarily detached homes and townhomes with modern plumbing and 200A electrical. Easiest renovation environment.
- **Murrayville and Brookswood (1970s–1990s)**: Established suburban communities with full-sized lots, good-condition homes, and increasingly popular for full renovations.
- **Aldergrove and Fort Langley**: Older communities (1950s–1980s) with character; some older electrical and plumbing.
- **Walnut Grove (1990s–2000s)**: Large detached homes in good condition, popular for kitchen and bathroom renovations.

**City of Langley:**
- Dense urban core along Fraser Highway with a mix of older homes (1940s–1970s) and newer condo developments. The character Nicomekl River area has some of Langley''s most interesting renovation projects.

## Bathroom Renovation Costs in Langley (2026)

### Budget Bathroom Refresh: $12,000–$21,000

For Langley''s newer Willoughby and Walnut Grove homes where the layout is good:

- Tub/shower re-tile: $2,800–$5,500
- New vanity (stock or semi-custom): $1,800–$3,800
- Toilet replacement: $450–$900
- Flooring tile: $1,100–$2,300
- Ventilation upgrade: $400–$800

**Note on newer homes**: Willoughby Heights homes built after 2005 typically have excellent plumbing (PEX) and electrical (200A), making bathroom renovations straightforward — no infrastructure surprises.

### Mid-Range Full Bathroom Renovation: $21,000–$36,000

The most popular renovation scope for Langley''s owner-occupied detached homes:

- Full gut and rebuild (everything out):
- New tile throughout (floor + walls): $4,000–$7,500
- Semi-custom or custom vanity: $2,500–$5,500
- Walk-in shower conversion (replacing tub): $4,500–$9,000
- Heated floors: $1,600–$3,200
- Toilet (comfort height): $500–$1,100
- New fixtures and accessories: $600–$1,200
- Township/City of Langley building permit: $260–$580

**Murrayville/Brookswood note**: 1970s–1990s Langley homes often have galvanized supply lines. If your shower pressure is weak or water discoloration occurs, budget $2,500–$5,000 for supply line replacement from main to fixtures during the bathroom renovation.

### High-End Primary Bathroom: $36,000–$62,000

For Langley''s executive homes in Brookswood, Walnut Grove, and Fort Langley acreage:

- Freestanding soaker tub: $3,000–$7,000
- Walk-in shower with frameless glass: $5,000–$10,000
- Custom double vanity: $5,000–$11,000
- Heated floors (electric or hydronic): $2,500–$5,500
- Large-format designer tile: $5,000–$10,000
- Steam shower system: $3,500–$7,500
- Towel warmers and accessories: $800–$2,000

## Secondary Bathroom and Ensuite Combinations

In Langley''s larger detached homes, many homeowners renovate both the main bathroom and the primary ensuite simultaneously — achieving project efficiencies (one mobilization, coordinated permits, consistent material sourcing):

**Dual bathroom renovation package estimate**: $38,000–$65,000 for a main bathroom + ensuite renovation, compared to $23,000–$41,000 if done separately. Typical savings from combining: $2,000–$5,000.

## Township and City of Langley Permit Requirements (2026)

**Important**: The Township of Langley and the City of Langley have separate building departments. Check which municipality your property falls in.

**Permit required for:**
- Moving or adding plumbing fixtures
- New electrical circuits or panel upgrades
- Structural modifications
- Gas line work

**No permit required for:**
- Toilet replacement (same location)
- Vanity replacement (same plumbing connections)
- Tile replacement (non-structural)
- Painting

**2026 permit fees:**

*Township of Langley:*
- Minor bathroom: $240–$500
- Bathroom with plumbing changes: $340–$720
- Structural: $650–$1,400

*City of Langley:*
- Minor bathroom: $260–$540
- Bathroom with plumbing: $360–$760

**Processing time**: Typically 2–4 weeks for both jurisdictions. The Township of Langley has an efficient online permit portal.

## Strata Bathrooms in Langley

Langley''s growing townhome inventory (particularly in Willoughby and Walnut Grove) includes many strata-governed properties. For strata bathroom renovations:

1. Written strata council approval required before work begins
2. Contractor credentials: WCB clearance + $2M liability insurance
3. Typically 4–8 weeks for council approval
4. Protect common hallways during material delivery
5. No work on weekends in most Langley stratas

**Townhome tip**: Many Willoughby townhomes have back-to-back bathrooms on upper floors sharing a plumbing wall. Any work on one bathroom''s supply or drain lines may affect the neighbouring unit''s plumbing — we coordinate with the strata and adjacent owners proactively. Older Metro Vancouver homes may also need our [Poly-B Pipe Replacement](/en/services/poly-b-replacement/) service to eliminate unsafe plastic piping.

## Related Resources

- [Bathroom Renovation Cost Vancouver 2026](/en/guides/bathroom-renovation-cost-vancouver/) — Metro Vancouver bathroom cost comparison
- [Kitchen Renovation Cost Vancouver 2026](/en/guides/kitchen-renovation-cost-vancouver/) — kitchen renovation planning
- [Renovation Services in Langley](/en/areas/langley/) — full Reno Stars service listing for Langley
- [Basement Renovation Cost Vancouver 2026](/en/guides/basement-renovation-cost-vancouver/) — basement suite options for Langley''s larger homes



For homeowners planning for the future or needing improved mobility, our [accessible bathroom renovations](/services/accessible-bathroom/) service includes grab bars, walk-in showers, wider doorways, and slip-resistant flooring.


Renovations that add appliances, EV charging, or high-draw fixtures often require a [critical load panel upgrade](/services/critical-load-panel/) — ensuring your home''s electrical system meets modern demand safely.


As part of a major renovation, many homeowners explore [heat pump HVAC upgrades](/services/heat-pump-hvac/) — an energy-efficient alternative to conventional heating and cooling that qualifies for significant BC Hydro and federal CleanBC rebates.
## Frequently Asked Questions

**How much does a bathroom renovation cost in Langley in 2026?**
Budget bathroom refreshes in Langley: $12,000–$21,000. Mid-range full renovations: $21,000–$36,000. High-end primary bathrooms: $36,000–$62,000.

**Is my Langley property in the Township or the City?**
Check your property tax notice or BC Assessment record. Willoughby, Murrayville, Brookswood, Fort Langley, Walnut Grove, and Aldergrove are in the Township. The City of Langley is the small urban core along Fraser Highway between 200th and 208th Streets.

**What''s the biggest mistake Langley homeowners make with bathroom renovations?**
Not replacing galvanized supply lines during a full renovation. If you''re already gutting the bathroom, it''s the perfect time to replace supply lines to copper or PEX — adding $1,500–$3,000 now prevents a $5,000–$8,000 emergency pipe repair later.

**Can Reno Stars do bathroom renovations in Willoughby?**
Yes — Willoughby Heights is one of our highest-volume service areas. We''ve completed dozens of bathroom renovations in Willoughby townhomes and detached homes, and we''re familiar with the Township of Langley permit process.

**How long does a Langley bathroom renovation take?**
Budget refreshes: 2–4 weeks. Mid-range full renovations: 4–7 weeks (including 2–4 weeks for permit). High-end primary bathrooms: 6–10 weeks. Strata projects add 4–8 weeks for council approval. See our guide to [BC Strata Renovation Rules](/en/blog/strata-renovation-rules-vancouver/) for Metro Vancouver homeowners.

**What bathroom renovation delivers the best pre-sale value in Langley?**
A tub-to-shower conversion is the highest-ROI pre-sale bathroom renovation in Langley. Converting a dated tub-only or tub/shower combo to a walk-in frameless glass shower — costing $14,000–$22,000 — addresses the single most common buyer objection in Langley''s family home market. Paired with a new vanity, tile throughout, and updated fixtures, this scope delivers strong perceived-value uplift in Willoughby and Walnut Grove homes priced $800,000–$1,200,000 where buyers compare multiple listings.



