Metro Vancouver realtors consistently prioritize: (1) **Kitchen** for homes where the kitchen is visually dated or has a poor layout — it''s the primary selling feature in 70% of buyer searches; (2) **Primary bathroom** if the kitchen is acceptable but the ensuite is outdated; (3) **Main bathroom** when there are children in the buyer profile; (4) **Flooring** across the whole main floor when the biggest visual deficiency is dated carpet or vinyl. The realtor''s standard advice: don''t over-renovate one room while leaving another dated — buyers discount for the weakest link, not the best room.

### How long do kitchen vs. bathroom renovations take in Vancouver?

Renovation timelines in Metro Vancouver: **Kitchen** — no permit needed (cosmetic): 4–6 weeks; with permit (plumbing/electrical changes): 8–14 weeks including permit processing. Older Metro Vancouver homes may also need our [Poly-B Pipe Replacement](/en/services/poly-b-replacement/) service to eliminate unsafe plastic piping. **Bathroom** — no permit (cosmetic fixture swap): 2–3 weeks; full renovation with permit: 6–10 weeks. The longest element in both: permit processing (4–14 weeks depending on city and complexity). Reno Stars mitigates this by submitting permit applications while clients are still finalizing selections — permits are often ready before construction starts.

### Which Vancouver renovation causes more daily disruption — kitchen or bathroom?

Kitchen renovations cause significantly higher daily disruption than bathroom renovations in Vancouver. During a kitchen renovation (4–8 weeks), residents cannot use the kitchen for cooking — meals require takeout or temporary cooking arrangements, which adds $100–$300/week to the real cost of the project. During a bathroom renovation (2–8 weeks), most households can manage using an alternate bathroom or scheduling around work hours. Homes with only one bathroom require more careful planning; temporary portable toilet options exist, but scheduling work to complete sections in stages is more practical.

