UPDATE blog_posts SET content_en = 'White Rock is one of Metro Vancouver''s most picturesque communities — a seaside city perched above the Semiahmoo Bay, famous for its beachfront promenade, oceanfront dining, and the iconic white rock on the shoreline. For homeowners, White Rock offers a unique renovation context: a mix of 1960s–1980s single-family homes on the hillside, newer condos near the town centre, and some of Metro Vancouver''s most dramatic ocean-view lots. This guide covers kitchen renovation costs, permit requirements, and what makes White Rock unique for renovation planning.

## White Rock Housing Stock

- **Hillside single-family homes (1960s–1990s)**: The majority of White Rock''s housing stock — typically 3-bedroom, 2-bathroom homes on sloped lots with ocean or mountain views. These often have original galvanized or copper plumbing and 100–150A electrical panels. Our [Critical Load Panel Installation](/en/services/critical-load-panel/) service upgrades your home electrical capacity for modern renovation demands.
- **Ocean-view luxury homes**: High-value properties on Marine Drive and the hillside above the promenade — premium renovation budgets, often involving sweeping view maximization and high-end finishes.
- **Condos and strata townhomes (2000s–present)**: The Johnston Road and Pacific Avenue corridors have newer strata developments. See our guide to [BC Strata Renovation Rules](/en/blog/strata-renovation-rules-vancouver/) for Metro Vancouver homeowners. White Rock is part of the City of White Rock, a small municipality with its own building department.
- **Older ranchers**: Some flat-lot areas south of Johnston Road have 1950s–1960s rancher-style homes with smaller kitchen footprints.

## Kitchen Renovation Costs in White Rock (2026)

### Budget Kitchen Renovation: $16,000–$27,000

For hillside family homes looking to refresh the existing layout:

- Cabinet refacing or semi-custom replacement: $4,500–$8,000
- Laminate or entry-level quartz countertops: $3,000–$5,800
- Tile backsplash: $1,200–$2,500
- Sink, faucet, and disposal: $600–$1,200
- Standard appliance package: $3,000–$6,000
- Under-cabinet lighting and new outlets: $900–$1,800

**Coastal humidity note**: White Rock''s oceanfront location means higher humidity than inland communities. Kitchen ventilation is especially important — budget for a higher-CFM hood fan ($800–$2,500 vs. Consider our [Heat Pump Installation Vancouver](/en/services/heat-pump-hvac/) service to upgrade heating and cooling with modern energy-efficient systems. standard $300–$800) and ensure adequate vapour barrier installation in any wet areas.

### Mid-Range Kitchen Renovation: $27,000–$46,000

Full kitchen replacement for White Rock''s hillside family homes:

- Semi-custom cabinetry: $11,000–$19,000
- Quartz countertops (with island): $5,500–$10,000
- Kitchen island: $3,000–$6,500
- Appliance package (mid-tier): $5,500–$11,000
- Plumbing: $1,200–$3,000
- Electrical: $1,200–$2,800
- City of White Rock building permit: $380–$820

### High-End Kitchen Renovation: $46,000–$85,000

Ocean-view homes on Marine Drive often command premium renovations with view-maximizing window extensions and high-end finishes:

- Custom cabinetry (view-framing design): $22,000–$38,000
- Natural stone countertops: $8,000–$16,000
- Professional appliance package: $10,000–$22,000
