UPDATE blog_posts SET content_en = '<h2>Introduction</h2><p>In the heart of [Surrey](/en/areas/surrey/), BC, a family sought to transform their outdated kitchen into a modern, functional space that would serve as the centerpiece of their home. This case study explores how Reno Stars took on the challenge and delivered a stunning [kitchen renovation](/en/services/kitchen/) | [Cabinet Refinishing](/en/services/cabinet/).</p><h2>Project Overview</h2><p>The project involved a complete overhaul of the kitchen space, including new flooring and modern finishes. The design featured plywood cabinetry, matching crown molding, sleek silver faucets, and elegant quartz countertops. With a budget of over $25,000 and a timeline of 4-5 weeks, the goal was to create a contemporary and functional cooking area for the family.</p><h3>Scope of Work</h3><ul><li>Cabinet Installation</li><li>Countertop Replacement</li><li>Backsplash Tiling</li><li>Plumbing</li><li>Lighting</li></ul><h2>Challenges</h2><p>One of the main challenges was ensuring the new design met the family''s functional needs while maintaining an aesthetic appeal. The family desired a space that was both practical for everyday use and stylish enough to impress guests.</p><h2>Our Solution</h2><p>To address this, we collaborated closely with the family to understand their preferences and incorporated practical solutions into the design. This collaboration ensured a balance between functionality and style, resulting in a kitchen that met all of the family''s needs.</p><h2>Before & After</h2><div><img src="https://pub-b88db8c50fd64a9a87f60a4486a4a488.r2.dev/uploads/admin/social-before-1-mmmlwpla.jpg" alt="Kitchen Renovation - Before Renovation 1"><img src="https://pub-b88db8c50fd64a9a87f60a4486a4a488.r2.dev/uploads/admin/social-after-1-mmmlwpla.jpg" alt="Elegant dining area featuring a wooden table, stylish chairs, and modern lighting."></div><div><img src="https://pub-b88db8c50fd64a9a87f60a4486a4a488.r2.dev/uploads/admin/social-before-2-mmmlwqa4.jpg" alt="Kitchen Renovation - Before Renovation 2"><img src="https://pub-b88db8c50fd64a9a87f60a4486a4a488.r2.dev/uploads/admin/social-after-2-mmmlwqa5.jpg" alt="Modern kitchen with white cabinetry, marble countertops, and stainless steel appliances."></div><h2>Results & Key Takeaways</h2><p>The final outcome was a modern kitchen that perfectly balanced style and functionality. The family was thrilled with the transformation, praising the sleek design and practical layout. This project highlights the importance of understanding client needs and delivering tailored solutions that exceed expectations.</p>



Metro Vancouver homeowners increasingly include a [heat pump HVAC upgrade](/services/heat-pump-hvac/) in their renovation plans — these systems provide efficient heating and cooling year-round, and qualify for BC Hydro and CleanBC rebate programs.


For homeowners planning long-term or accommodating family members with mobility needs, [accessible bathroom renovations](/services/accessible-bathroom/) — including grab bars, curbless showers, and slip-resistant flooring — are a smart addition to any major renovation project.


If you live in a strata property (condo or townhouse), review BC''s [strata renovation rules](/blog/strata-renovation-rules-vancouver/) before starting work — many projects require strata council approval and must follow specific noise, hour, and contractor requirements.
## Frequently Asked Questions

### How much did this Surrey [kitchen renovation cost](/en/guides/kitchen-renovation-cost-vancouver/)?
This Surrey kitchen renovation for a family home was designed to transform an outdated kitchen into a modern, functional centerpiece. Surrey kitchen renovations at mid-range finish level typically cost $22,000–$45,000 for a complete transformation including new cabinetry, countertops, backsplash, sink and faucet, lighting, and permit-required electrical. This project demonstrates how a well-planned kitchen renovation can serve as the centerpiece of a family home while remaining within a realistic budget for Surrey''s housing market.

### What is the renovation process for a [Surrey kitchen project](/en/blog/kitchen-renovation-surrey-bc-2026/)?
A Surrey kitchen renovation follows a structured process: (1) design consultation and selections (2–3 weeks), (2) permit application to City of Surrey (3–5 weeks, can run parallel to cabinet ordering), (3) demolition of existing kitchen (1–2 days), (4) plumbing and electrical rough-in with inspections (3–5 days), (5) cabinet installation (2–3 days), (6) countertop template, fabrication, and installation (2–3 weeks), (7) tile backsplash installation (2–3 days), (8) plumbing fixtures and appliance connection (1–2 days), (9) final cleanup and punch list (1 day).

### What kitchen design choices work best for Surrey family homes?
Surrey family kitchens benefit most from: maximum storage (deep pantry cabinets, drawer base units instead of door base units where possible, upper cabinets to ceiling height), durable surfaces (quartz countertops resist staining from family cooking, LVP or tile flooring handles high-traffic better than hardwood), a large sink (single basin or large double basin for cleaning large pots), and practical lighting (under-cabinet task lighting and bright overhead pot lights for visibility during cooking). Design aesthetics should be clean and neutral to maximize broad appeal at resale.

### How long does a kitchen renovation take in Surrey, BC?
A complete Surrey kitchen renovation takes 8–14 weeks from contract signing to a functional new kitchen. Cabinet selection and ordering: 1–2 weeks. City of Surrey permit: 3–5 weeks (concurrent with cabinet manufacturing for custom/semi-custom). Active construction after permit and cabinet delivery: 5–8 weeks. Stock IKEA cabinet projects move faster: 6–10 weeks total. Having appliances, sink, faucet, and backsplash tile selected before construction begins prevents scheduling hold-ups between trade phases.

### Is kitchen renovation the best investment in a Surrey home?
Kitchen renovations consistently deliver the highest combination of resale ROI and quality-of-life improvement in Surrey homes. In Surrey''s $1.1M–$1.7M detached home market, a dated kitchen is the primary buyer objection and a modern kitchen is the single feature most mentioned in positive listing reviews. A $25,000–$45,000 kitchen renovation in a Surrey home typically adds $35,000–$65,000 in perceived market value at resale, while immediately improving how the family uses their home every day. For expert [Pre-Sale Renovation Advice](/en/services/realtor/) before listing, speak with our renovation team.

### Does a kitchen renovation in Surrey, BC require a building permit?
Yes — City of Surrey requires a building permit for any kitchen renovation involving plumbing changes (relocating a sink or adding a gas line), electrical upgrades (new dedicated circuits for appliances), or structural modifications (removing a wall). Our [Critical Load Panel Installation](/en/services/critical-load-panel/) service upgrades your home electrical capacity for modern renovation demands. Older Metro Vancouver homes may also need our [Poly-B Pipe Replacement](/en/services/poly-b-replacement/) service to eliminate unsafe plastic piping. Surrey permit applications typically take 3–5 weeks to process and can be submitted concurrently with cabinet ordering to avoid schedule delays. The contractor handles the permit submission on most full renovation projects. Cosmetic-only work — replacing cabinet doors, countertops, backsplash tile, and appliances in the same locations — does not require a permit.

See our [verified five-star reviews](/en/reviews/) from Metro Vancouver homeowners.

