<p>These numbers come from real Reno Stars projects in Burnaby — not industry surveys or estimator tools. Every line includes labour, materials, permits, garbage removal, and a 3-year workmanship warranty.</p>
<h2>Real Burnaby projects: what we built and what it cost</h2>
<h3>Custom Kitchen Renovation with Wood Veins Cabinets — $30,000 – $35,000</h3>
<p>A Burnaby townhouse kitchen transformed with wood-grain cabinets, a contrasting island, and quartz countertops. Smart layout planning maximized every square foot, and updated lighting completely changed the feel of the space. Full project link in our <a href="/projects/kitchen-renovation">Burnaby kitchen projects collection</a>.</p>
<h3>Custom Kitchen Renovation with Gold Fixtures — $35,000 – $40,000</h3>
<p>A higher-end Burnaby kitchen renovation with custom cabinets and gold hardware accents. The owner wanted a unique look that still functioned for a busy family. We coordinated cabinet manufacturing, plumbing, electrical, and tile work in a 6-week timeline.</p>
<h3>Luxury Bathroom Renovation with Custom Features — $28,000 – $32,000</h3>
<p>A Burnaby home&#39;s master bathroom redone with custom tile work, a frameless glass shower, and integrated lighting. The luxury bracket in Burnaby usually means custom glass + premium fixtures + niche lighting — every one of those adds $1,000-$2,000.</p>
<h3>Two Bathroom Renovation with Custom Features in Burnaby — $26,000 – $30,000</h3>
<p>Two bathrooms tackled in parallel for a Burnaby family. Doing both at once cuts ~15% off the combined cost vs sequential renovations because demolition, plumbing, and tile crews work back-to-back instead of mobilizing twice.</p>
